INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1124,'en','Take an old worn bow, dust it with magical cure, ask a dragon to blow on it and you''ll have an enchanted bow. Be careful however, theorizing on fairy recipes is all very well, but in practice, dragons take a malicious pleasure in blowing on everything but the bow.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1125,'en','This unconventional bow has been created for the self-proclaimed king of a village of lowly peasants, who liked to show off by shooting two arrows at once.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1126,'en','This unconventional bow has been created for the self-proclaimed king of a village of lowly peasants, who liked to show off by shooting two arrows at once.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1127,'en','This unconventional bow has been created for the self-proclaimed king of a village of lowly peasants, who liked to show off by shooting two arrows at once.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1128,'en','This unconventional bow has been created for the self-proclaimed king of a village of lowly peasants, who liked to show off by shooting two arrows at once.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1131,'en','This heavy Wand shattered more than one soul''s skull. Iop priests use it to send repentant sinners to heaven with a bang.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1132,'en','It''s the symbol of purity and... stupidity. Just like its creator who nevertheless gave it tremendous magic powers.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1133,'en','This stick was the key to the emancipation of the Eniripsa housewives: a fearsome weapon against both monsters and hard-to-reach dust.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1134,'en','This stick was the key to the emancipation of the Eniripsa housewives: a fearsome weapon against both monsters and hard-to-reach dust.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1135,'en','This stick was the key to the emancipation of the Eniripsa housewives: a fearsome weapon against both monsters and hard-to-reach dust.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1136,'en','This stick was the key to the emancipation of the Eniripsa housewives: a fearsome weapon against both monsters and hard-to-reach dust.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1137,'en','Houvette invented these wands to claim back her Enutrof husband from the liquid grip of the bar where he spent his evenings. She also used them to spice up their relationship, but nobody knows exactly how...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1138,'en','Houvette invented these wands to claim back her Enutrof husband from the liquid grip of the bar where he spent his evenings. She also used them to spice up their relationship, but nobody knows exactly how...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1139,'en','Houvette invented these wands to claim back her Enutrof husband from the liquid grip of the bar where he spent his evenings. She also used them to spice up their relationship, but nobody knows exactly how...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1140,'en','Houvette invented these wands to claim back her Enutrof husband from the liquid grip of the bar where he spent his evenings. She also used them to spice up their relationship, but nobody knows exactly how...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1143,'en','According to the tag, this wand has the power to make people obey whoever is holding it. The instructions say you have to shake it rapidly near your adversary. If it doesn''t work, try and poke him in the eye with it.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1144,'en','According to the tag, this wand has the power to make people obey whoever is holding it. The instructions say you have to shake it rapidly near your adversary. If it doesn''t work, try and poke him in the eye with it.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1145,'en','According to the tag, this wand has the power to make people obey whoever is holding it. The instructions say you have to shake it rapidly near your adversary. If it doesn''t work, try and poke him in the eye with it.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1146,'en','According to the tag, this wand has the power to make people obey whoever is holding it. The instructions say you have to shake it rapidly near your adversary. If it doesn''t work, try and poke him in the eye with it.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1147,'en','This staff is a replica of a legendary artefact, but with slightly lesser powers. It sends out light if it falls on the ground and it can distort your voice to any pitch you desire. The latter feature is useful for luring enemies into mortal traps... just don''t try to kill them with it when they fall for your trick.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1148,'en','Most young Fecas have staffs quite similar to this one. More than a fashion, it''s almost become a ritual. Has no one ever told them how ridiculous they look?');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1149,'en','Most young Fecas have staffs quite similar to this one. More than a fashion, it''s almost become a ritual. Has no one ever told them how ridiculous they look?');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1150,'en','Most young Fecas have staffs quite similar to this one. More than a fashion, it''s almost become a ritual. Has no one ever told them how ridiculous they look?');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1151,'en','Most young Fecas have staffs quite similar to this one. More than a fashion, it''s almost become a ritual. Has no one ever told them how ridiculous they look?');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1152,'en','A short-sighted, grumbling, fortune telling, smelly old Feca accidentally created this powerful weapon when her staff rammed into her crystal ball as she slipped from the kitchen table. She''d read her own fortune long before and, well, she more or less lived on that table... wonder what it was she thought was going to kill her... well, I guess she wasn''t the best fortune teller.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1153,'en','A short-sighted, grumbling, fortune telling, smelly old Feca accidentally created this powerful weapon when her staff rammed into her crystal ball as she slipped from the kitchen table. She''d read her own fortune long before and, well, she more or less lived on that table... wonder what it was she thought was going to kill her... well, I guess she wasn''t the best fortune teller.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1154,'en','A short-sighted, grumbling, fortune telling, smelly old Feca accidentally created this powerful weapon when her staff rammed into her crystal ball as she slipped from the kitchen table. She''d read her own fortune long before and, well, she more or less lived on that table... wonder what it was she thought was going to kill her... well, I guess she wasn''t the best fortune teller.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1157,'en','A short-sighted, grumbling, fortune telling, smelly old Feca accidentally created this powerful weapon when her staff rammed into her crystal ball as she slipped from the kitchen table. She''d read her own fortune long before and, well, she more or less lived on that table... wonder what it was she thought was going to kill her... well, I guess she wasn''t the best fortune teller.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1161,'en','The success of the Wa Wabbit Staff lead to the creation of a host of cheap copies. Today, there are far more fakes than originals.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1162,'en','The success of the Wa Wabbit Staff lead to the creation of a host of cheap copies. Today, there are far more fakes than originals.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1163,'en','The success of the Wa Wabbit Staff lead to the creation of a host of cheap copies. Today, there are far more fakes than originals.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1164,'en','The success of the Wa Wabbit Staff lead to the creation of a host of cheap copies. Today, there are far more fakes than originals.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1330,'en','It is an original creation of the silversmith John-Lay Nonne, and now one of the most sought after jewels on the continent.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1331,'en','Oly was a female Iop with only one ability - cooking. It is said that Iop himself gave her this medal in order to compensate for her weaknesses in battle. Only pure-hearted people can wear it.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1350,'en','This bow was created by a wizard who was fond of his cider. In order to ease his crippling hangovers, he invented this water-type bow.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1351,'en','As the saying goes "With a bow, it''s make or break". Wise men avoid this bow. The rumour is it has the evil eye...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1352,'en','This bow carries the forces of earth and water. Woe betide him who cannot control at least one of the two...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1353,'en','All the pulleys of this bow were sawn off. It used to be a symbol of the conflict between Good and Evil.
Touch it and you''ll feel the supreme justice of the ancient lawmakers running through your fingertips.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1354,'en','Hick was an accursed Cra: he couldn''t stop hiccupping... One day he threw his bow into the fire and decided to use a sword instead. The curse strangely disappeared at that exact moment...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1355,'en','The man who created this bow, a certain Marc Hidsad, never really knew how to use it. He usually hurt himself just as much as his enemies.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1356,'en','Rika Zarouil The Female Baker was renowned for having been the smallest Eniripsa in the whole world of Amakna. She made her loaves in small cardboard furnaces and used this old bread to impale many a hero.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1357,'en','A mischievous sculptor tried to make people think his wands were daggers, calling them Wangers at first, and then simply Wangs. His plan didn''t work, but his wands most definitely do.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1359,'en','The origins of this wand remain quite obscure. I can tell you that it''s great for finding parking on a rainy Monday in Amakna town... Just points in the direction you need to go... It does one-way streets and everything!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1360,'en','This wand was created many years ago in the forging flames of Dyin Ard. You''d be well-advised to have a bucket of water at hand just to keep control of the mini-inferno.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1361,'en','The Sylvian Wand gives you sharp sight. You''ll probably use it for picking out a good escape route.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1362,'en','The Vampiric Stake is in fact the wand of a vampire who retired long ago from social life and slaughtering. This strange piece of wood has nevertheless inherited a few qualities from its former owner...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1363,'en','On top of its unbearable name, this staff has many ways to get on its owner''s nerves.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1364,'en','This staff is just great... Gets rid of all your worries and bad vibes for a whole day... Along with about six weeks of your memory... And most of your... Okay, maybe it''s not such a good idea.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1365,'en','They say it was the staff that made a fearsome warrior of Heds, they say it was magic and could shoot fire. Ever heard of All Bran? Eight bowls of this stuff a day and you''d be shooting fire too buddy...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1366,'en','This staff is commonly used by gobbherds during the trading season to fend off the Bworks, who like to snack on the Gobball herds around this time. The prized dish is the gobbherd himself.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1367,'en','This staff once belonged to the beautiful Dina Mite, renowned for her explosive voice... In her day, she was a cracker too.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1368,'en','"The 110" was the name given to the 110 Amakna firemen who, in the year 450, valiantly fought the fire started by a bored Red Wyrmling. This spear belonged to one of them and will only respond to valiant hands.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1369,'en','These knives have been specially conceived to be used in luxury restaurants. However, because of their rather strange appearance, the owner decided to resell them to a travelling knife thrower.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1370,'en','The hilt of this weapon is greasy and slippery but it really does look fab.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1371,'en','Eulasse was a gobbherd in Amakna who one day found these dirty daggers in the Gobball dung heap. Be careful with them, the hilts are still a bit slippery...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1372,'en','Otof''Mai''We was a hermit, a legendary disciple of Sram, who spent his life avoiding all sorts of contact with others. When he died, his favourite daggers were found next to his body. Only the nimblest of men can control them.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1373,'en','Any Enutrof worthy of the name has a beard and old Krys Nosheive was no exception. One day his wife, Mrs Nosheive, bought him a razor, and he decided he would rather use it as a weapon.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1374,'en','Tylo was an ancient scribe of Amakna... centuries ago. He had the strange habit of carving stone using daggers instead of chisels. This magnificent and resistant dagger belonged to him.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1375,'en','Terophyle the Iop was capable of lifting enormous stones... It''s not really proof of intelligence to you or I, but a Iop who can capture the idea of picking up something round is already a king among his people.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1376,'en','This axe might be heavy, but it will take down Trools in a flash. The magic runes it contains can also burn enemies.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1377,'en','Hure was a young priest who used weapons freely to spread the word of God. His favourite weapon was an axe on which he inscribed numerous meaningful quotations... his final blows were always accompanied by a blood-curdling supplications, which ended, each word like a hot pin in the victim''s ear, with the phrase "And, you will know my name is The Lord when I lay my vengeance upon thee!"');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1378,'en','Created for young, bloodthirsty warriors, this battle axe makes a deafening noise when it strikes another weapon.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1379,'en','Legend has it that the name of this hammer is in fact the phonetic transcription of the noise it makes when it crushes a skull. Unfortunately, it is impossible to be sure since anyone within earshot tends not to make it out alive.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1383,'en','It took many, many years and many, many smiths to forge this hammer. The result is a magnificent weapon which has unfortunately inherited a particular concept of efficiency from its creators.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1393,'en','This Hammer was made from a clock, the famous clock swallowed by the Crocodyl when it devoured the hand of Captain Hawkfish. Though the clock has been located, the hand is still missing. Hawkfish''s hand that is... the clock was in surprisingly good... Oh forget it.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1399,'en','Just like the amulet of the same name, the Aclou Mallet can transform your vital energy into strength. To be taken in moderation.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1403,'en','This hammer once belonged to Aha, a young Osamodas who wasted all his days telling painful one-liners. The hammer couldn''t break open a hazelnut, but it''s useful for breaking the ice from time to time.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1404,'en','So you like animals? So did Toh''Lo. He devoted his whole life to helping them out. This hammer kind of represents his relationship with animals, a communion as shaky as a lame Gobball on a freshly gravelled driveway.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1426,'en','Layte, the creator of this shovel, was a devoted disciple of Iop. You can guess what this guy''s major flaw was.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1427,'en','This shovel is used by the Kanniball High Priests of Moon Island to invoke Zebuth, one of their gods who is often depicted as a cow. Only vile characters use it.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1429,'en','This shovel, created by Mechba, is used by Enutrof followers to knock nuts from trees. On the battlefield, it has a similar function. Yowza!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1430,'en','This shovel, created by Mechba, is used by Enutrof followers to knock nuts from trees. On the battlefield, it has a similar function. Yowza!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1431,'en','This shovel, created by Mechba, is used by Enutrof followers to knock nuts from trees. On the battlefield, it has a similar function. Yowza!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1432,'en','Gaston Houze, gardener and disciple of Enutrof, planted too many plants. It had to be said... There, I''ve said it. What''s more this worn spade is the evidence of his dirty business. Never talk to this thing, it''ll tell you stories, don''t believe a word, it''ll have you digging yourself into your own grave before you know it... and then where will you be? I hate this damn thing.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1433,'en','This shovel was once a self-defence weapon used by a small group of female Enutrof''s followers. Once they had even this puny pile of power in their clutches, they turned into horrible crea.......');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1435,'en','Very heavy shovel. For fa...um, big boned adventurers.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1436,'en','Ikan was Churros the Warrior''s little fish. The shovel doesn''t look a thing like the creature, but the smell is almost identical...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1438,'en','This pick is considered a lucky charm, although anyone depending on a pick to make their living has usually seen that boat sail a long time ago.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1439,'en','This pick seems to bring the evil eye upon you. With a few alterations here and there, perhaps you could have a great pick on your hands.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1474,'en','This ultra-powerful amulet is the fruit of the expert time-mastery of an old Xelor.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1475,'en','The Pretty Blade has been crafted by the renowned blacksmith Dave-LoL, just before he died for the sake of the prettiest girl in the kingdom, a Iop. It is said that the efficiency of the blade is only matched by the grace of the wearer.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1476,'en','This powerful pendant contains the life-blood of the Crackler, that is to say all the items he gathered before he was killed by some jealous adventurer.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1477,'en','Mulette was a little female Ecaflip dogged by bad luck... until her grandmother presented her with this amulet.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1478,'en','This pendant will make you feel more harmonious.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1479,'en','This legendary Hammer has already proved itself in Amakna. It belonged to the powerful Cardboard Twot who used it to transform his opponents into confetti and papier-mâché.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1480,'en','This pendant will make you feel at peace with the world.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1481,'en','This pendant will make you grant you greater understanding of the world around you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1482,'en','This is an extremely useful amulet, but it turns its wearer as white as a Gobball.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1483,'en','A mysterious symbol of a mysterious organization... by the way, it doesn''t exist and you''ve never heard of it, understand?');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1484,'en','An excellent copy of the work done by Polma Kartnay, the silversmith''s apprentice. This reproduction surpasses the original.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1485,'en','This amulet is said to be a modified version of the Golden Destiny... which is really strange when you think that these two amulets have nothing in common except their ridiculous appearance.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1486,'en','Holy was a female Iop, intent on spreading Evil throughout the land. Renowned for her incredible composure, she would never get angry except when people compared her to someone named Oly.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1487,'en','Not only is this belt elegant, it also massages you as you walk... You''d be surprised what a back rub can do for your murderous instinct.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1488,'en','This strange name refers to an equally strange object made from previous amulets... goodness knows how. We know just as little about the circumstances in which it was found...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1489,'en','With this near-perfect pin, you''ll have the wisdom of an Irish salmon. It''s great for group therapy sessions among friends. Don''t forget to bring some tissues, though, it can get emotional!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1490,'en','The creator of this chain, someone called Ken Aton, was renowned for his strange habits. He spent all his time hunting the Minotoror for his coat which he wanted to make into an Asserag');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1491,'en','The Liche was a dirty creature known for infiltrating the ranks of valiant warriors in order to steal food. Marmalade and toast was his favourite. But one day, the warriors saw through its little game and the Liche had to run away...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1493,'en','It is said that this ring emerged out of a Sacrier''s grinning, pus-stuffed wound. Niiice.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1494,'en','The main function of this pretty ring was to help Osamodas recognize their Tofus during fights.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1495,'en','This small modest-looking ring was created by Degun. He was more famous for shouting his head off without the slightest reason and his violent aversion to the Liche than for his talent as a jeweller.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1496,'en','This ring was made to increase its wearers luck during card games.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1497,'en','Rings forged during Xelor''s temporal journeys.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1498,'en','These rings were cooled from the forge with the tears of Enutrof, shed over his lost shovel. Must have been some shovel!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1499,'en','This ring is meant for Enutrofs only. It was enchanted by their God so that the followers would be the only ones to wear it. It allows all god-fearing Enutrofs to be even luckier than usual in treasure hunts.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1500,'en','Made of many different fibres, this magnificent cloak is unique - just look at that patchwork of colour and the way the light plays on its surface.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1501,'en','With this wedding ring, you''ll satisfy the most mercenary of fathers-in-law.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1503,'en','It is said that to create this wand, it is put into a warm corpse, which is then buried shortly afterwards. No one dares to imagine by what route exactly the wand is put into the dead body.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1504,'en','Billy-Ray Red Neck was renowned throughout the countryside. One day, as he was yodelling at the top of his voice, someone cut off his head, which is why he got the nickname. The dagger was found but nobody looked for the murderer... Billy-Ray was famous for singing out of tune.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1511,'en','According to the legend describing the Dantesque fight after which he was raised to the rank of God himself, Ecaflip used a weapon made by the ancient principle: "a tail for a life". This series of swords was forged as a tribute to him.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1520,'en','This hammer impregnated with magic oil is essential to create magic items.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1539,'en','Hammer impregnated with magic oil, essential to create magic items.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1559,'en','This ring is in fact an outgrowth of the Soft Oak, uprooted during a storm. It''s now yours, but keep it away from its master as he could decide to take back what''s his!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1560,'en','Hammer impregnated with magic oil, essential to create magic items.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1561,'en','Hammer impregnated with magic oil, essential to create magic items.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1562,'en','This hammer impregnated with magic oil is essential to create magic items.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1563,'en','This dagger is impregnated with magic essence, essential for carving magic creations.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1564,'en','This dagger is impregnated with magic essence, essential for carving magic creations.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1565,'en','This dagger is impregnated with magic essence, essential for carving magic creations.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1574,'en','This sword belonged to the late lamented Kih Besans, known as the Yench Carver. This was his main hobby... Pointless to mention that some people waste their lives.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1602,'en','This ring allows the Dark Treechnid to be very stylish when it goes dancing. And as life is kind, there are many parties in the Dark Forest.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1619,'en','The Treemu is an elegant amulet. If you''re planning on putting it on, we advise you not to wear any other clothes, as it makes silk look like the wool off a Gobball''s backside.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1620,'en','This bow looks as if it were still alive and can almost shoot arrows on its own like a big boy. It could have been the perfect bow for people who are clumsy with their hands but, unfortunately, the arrow always has to be loaded the right way.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1621,'en','The Skill Boots increase agility and intelligence to the detriment of your strength and chance. Contrary to what many people believe, they won''t defeat your opponent for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1622,'en','These Power Boots increase strength and chance to the detriment of your intelligence and agility. Contrary to what many people believe, they won''t bring you incredible power.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1623,'en','The Anticipation Boots increase strength and agility to the detriment of your intelligence and chance. Contrary to what many people believe, these boots do not enable you to anticipate your enemies'' next moves.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1624,'en','These boots once belonged to the great knight Nexus - the poor bugger was frozen for eternity.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1628,'en','The story of this artefact originates from a very ancient legend but its real power is yet to be revealed.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1629,'en','The story of this artefact originates from a very ancient legend but its real power is yet to be revealed.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1630,'en','The story of this artefact originates from a very ancient legend but its real power is yet to be revealed.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1631,'en','The story of this artefact originates from a very ancient legend but its real power is yet to be revealed.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1632,'en','The story of this artefact originates from a very ancient legend but its real power is yet to be revealed.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1633,'en','The story of this artefact originates from a very ancient legend but its real power is yet to be revealed.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1636,'en','This sword was created by a glamorous young lady who wanted a weapon in her own image and endowed it with the her own graceful beauty and passionate nature. Have a look at this piece. Magnificent');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1637,'en','This sword was created by a glamorous young lady who wanted a weapon in her own image and endowed it with the her own graceful beauty and passionate nature. Have a look at this piece. Magnificent');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1638,'en','This sword was created by a glamorous young lady who wanted a weapon in her own image and endowed it with the her own graceful beauty and passionate nature. Have a look at this piece. Magnificent');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1639,'en','This sword was created by a glamorous young lady who wanted a weapon in her own image and endowed it with the her own graceful beauty and passionate nature. Have a look at this piece. Magnificent');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1640,'en','This sword is absolutely perfect for attacking the defenceless. Quick, handy and above all extremely sharp, it has been banned from the shops for many years now. It is tolerated only if used on Bworks.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1641,'en','This sword is absolutely perfect for attacking the defenceless. Quick, handy and above all extremely sharp, it has been banned from the shops for many years now. It is tolerated only if used on Bworks.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1650,'en','This sword is absolutely perfect for attacking the defenceless. Quick, handy and above all extremely sharp, it has been banned from the shops for many years now. It is tolerated only if used on Bworks.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1651,'en','This sword is absolutely perfect for attacking the defenceless. Quick, handy and above all extremely sharp, it has been banned from shops for many years now. It is tolerated only if used on Bworks.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1656,'en','This ring can protect you from weak magic attacks... In practice, from infantile monsters with something to prove.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1657,'en','This ring can protect you from weak magic attacks... In practice, from infantile monsters with something to prove.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1661,'en','Wearing a necklace with a Moskito encased in amber will show your opponents you''re a fearsome hunter... of Moskitoes! Unless you''re still a toddler, that''s got to be embarrassing.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1662,'en','Wearing an amber Arachnee around your neck when attacking one of its sisters can be enough to disconcert it. Poor bug though, it''s what we call the "irony of fate".');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1665,'en','These strange boots were first used by young disciples who were one or two socks short of a pair. Ah yes, popular with the Iops.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1666,'en','These boots have been especially made for those who prefer to watch their summons do all the hard work during fights.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1667,'en','This belt takes its name from its creator, a shoemaker who was less renowned and much older than Bowisse, but quite gifted all the same.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1668,'en','The Dodu was a Sadida who loved frightening his enemies. He asked Bowisse to make him a belt that matched the colour of his hair... Like many charmers, the Dodu had a rotten heart.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1669,'en','This belt was made for the most popular of all the Craettes who often organised parties and wacky events to keep her countless friends and acquaintances on her side. All this between ironing and washing Captain Chafer''s leather underpants.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1693,'en','The famous tailor, Jules Yanos, was particularly renowned for having exchanged his wife for a magic thimble. What a businessman, hmm? Just great!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1695,'en','Some say Captain Chafer tried to steal this cloak to replace his famous leather panties. But it didn''t suit him at all - it just wasn''t perverse enough.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1697,'en','Don''t expect this bag to make a hero of you. It will keep all your personal items in one place. Better than nothing, I suppose.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1698,'en','This bag is specially designed for holding the resources you collect. 
Only true harvesters can carry it. (level 20 in one of the harvesting professions required).');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1699,'en','This bag is ideal for those who never wander far from home but take useless things with them when they do. Like ash planks for example.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1700,'en','Designed by Tengra Reufrus, this aerodynamic belt will make you as nimble as a Tofu and as windy as the breeze. Or is it the opposite?');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1701,'en','This belt has small pockets allowing you to stock more items in your inventory.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1702,'en','This bag is specially designed for holding the resources you collect. 
Only true harvesters can carry it (level 40 in one of the harvesting professions required).');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1703,'en','This bag is specially designed for holding the resources you collect. 
Only true harvesters can carry it (level 60 in one of the harvesting professions required).');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1704,'en','Legend whispers of a miner who worked continuously for several months in 4 different mines simultaneously, raising a family in the process and running a successful one-man printing press with his feet... The Hammer-Sickle newspaper hard at work again...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1705,'en','It''s the ideal bag for holding all your bread and potions when you go away for several months... into the labyrinth for example.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1707,'en','It''s the ideal bag to keep all your bread and potions when you are on an exotic vacation...like in the Moon Island.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1710,'en','The origins of this crescent-shaped amulet, are known to only the very few... 
Who knows what might happen if you put it on...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1711,'en','Take this dog to the park, take him to the toilet, show him to your friends, but whatever you do - and please listen carefully - do not feed him. This pet will remove your arm up to the elbow. 
(THIS PET DOESN''T LIKE ANY RESOURCES)');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1718,'en','The powers given to this ring by the Dark Breath of Grougalorasalar are now considerably weakened. This relic was intended for Crocoburio, the only one capable of mastering it without being dominated himself.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1719,'en','This pair of boots apparently belonged to Crocoburio. Only a few people can put them on and they are immediately plunged into a clever, Machiavellian frame of mind. Legend has it that this evil spell is due to the numerous skulls the boots have crushed.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1720,'en','Grougalorasalar loved collecting the bone fragments of his most fearsome enemies. His affection for Crocoburio inspired the creation of this ultra-powerful belt.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1728,'en','The fairer sex of the fairest class will fall under the spell of this cuddly little ball of fluff. For this reason alone it''s to be avoided.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000008,'en','The fairer sex of the fairest class will fall under the spell of this cuddly little ball of fluff. For this reason alone it''s to be avoided.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000009,'en','The fairer sex of the fairest class will fall under the spell of this cuddly little ball of fluff. For this reason alone it''s to be avoided.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000010,'en','The fairer sex of the fairest class will fall under the spell of this cuddly little ball of fluff. For this reason alone it''s to be avoided.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000011,'en','The fairer sex of the fairest class will fall under the spell of this cuddly little ball of fluff. For this reason alone it''s to be avoided.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000012,'en','The fairer sex of the fairest class will fall under the spell of this cuddly little ball of fluff. For this reason alone it''s to be avoided.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000013,'en','The fairer sex of the fairest class will fall under the spell of this cuddly little ball of fluff. For this reason alone it''s to be avoided.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1729,'en','This ring once belonged to Mer, the laziest piece of stuff in Amakna. He worshipped doughnuts and ribs...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1739,'en','This wand is searingly hot to the touch. But the most enigmatic thing about it is its ash smell which would make you think it had survived a forest fire.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1748,'en','This little Wabbit is domesticated and won''t bite you. As for strangers, however...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000073,'en','This little Wabbit is domesticated and won''t bite you. As for strangers, however...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000074,'en','This little Wabbit is domesticated and won''t bite you. As for strangers, however...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000075,'en','This little Wabbit is domesticated and won''t bite you. As for strangers, however...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000076,'en','This little Wabbit is domesticated and won''t bite you. As for strangers, however...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000077,'en','This little Wabbit is domesticated and won''t bite you. As for strangers, however...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1904,'en','A White Dreggon Shell padded with leather and wool, this headgear will protect you against basic attacks and the lightning bolts of a stumbling, drunk Bwork Magus. You''ll also look like you just came out of a Dreggon''s backside.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1907,'en','These ears will accentuate your bright smile and get the opposite sex spreading rumours about you...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1908,'en','Even Spartapine the Great Reaper doesn''t have such a helmet, the precious stones and metals used to make it ensure your noggin will be kept safe and sound inside..');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(1910,'en','This cloak is made from the body parts of an Ouginak, it still has the smell of the creature''s humid nose. Personally, its taste reminds me of a horny set of Gobball''s udders... Well, someone told me that... damn...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2061,'en','This cloak, not really nice at first sight, is nevertheless really efficient. Once you get used to the smell of rotting Crow.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2063,'en','These boots are made from different parts of Crow carcasses. The wearer has a strange feeling of nimbleness comparable to that given by the traditional flying potion made with grilled boletus.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2066,'en','This is an approximate replica of a Kaniger''s staff. It holds many surprises in store - and they''re not all good.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2070,'en','This bone helmet has been in a Kaniger''s pocket for many years. Worn and scratched it might be, but its properties are as powerful as ever.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2074,'en','This cute little Bwak will soon become an ugly Kwak. No reason to be afraid until then, so keep it with you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000040,'en','This cute little Bwak will soon become an ugly Kwak. No reason to be afraid until then, so keep it with you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000041,'en','This cute little Bwak will soon become an ugly Kwak. No reason to be afraid until then, so keep it with you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000042,'en','This cute little Bwak will soon become an ugly Kwak. No reason to be afraid until then, so keep it with you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2075,'en','This cute little Bwak will soon become an ugly Kwak. No reason to be afraid until then, so keep it with you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000078,'en','This cute little Bwak will soon become an ugly Kwak. No reason to be afraid until then, so keep it with you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000079,'en','This cute little Bwak will soon become an ugly Kwak. No reason to be afraid until then, so keep it with you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000080,'en','This cute little Bwak will soon become an ugly Kwak. No reason to be afraid until then, so keep it with you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2076,'en','This cute little Bwak will soon become an ugly Kwak. No reason to be afraid until then, so keep it with you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000000,'en','This cute little Bwak will soon become an ugly Kwak. No reason to be afraid until then, so keep it with you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000001,'en','This cute little Bwak will soon become an ugly Kwak. No reason to be afraid until then, so keep it with you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000002,'en','This cute little Bwak will soon become an ugly Kwak. No reason to be afraid until then, so keep it with you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2077,'en','This cute little Bwak will soon become an ugly Kwak. No reason to be afraid until then, so keep it with you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000021,'en','This cute little Bwak will soon become an ugly Kwak. No reason to be afraid until then, so keep it with you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000022,'en','This cute little Bwak will soon become an ugly Kwak. No reason to be afraid until then, so keep it with you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000023,'en','This cute little Bwak will soon become an ugly Kwak. No reason to be afraid until then, so keep it with you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2094,'en','The Dark Makroute is a hat created from a Mutilated Makroute stitched together without an anaesthetic. Strangely enough, the master who visited these mutilations upon him is the only one it obeys... it can''t stand strangers.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2095,'en','The Bear is a hat made from a head of a dead bear. Its fur is still silky and warm. The tailor who made it must have been really skilled to keep the look of terror on the dead bear''s face.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2096,'en','Brave the Ghost was the first one to use Dark Wicker in fields other than gastronomy.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2097,'en','The Champo once belonged to one of the greatest Fungi Masters of Amakna. Valiant and brilliant, Gnion the Boletus was the only one of his race who gained the respect of Human beings.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2104,'en','The Daudgee is a disturbing Helmet, made of Ouginak remains and other rubbish. Worn for many years by Gourlo The Terrible, the Daudgee came to symbolise hopeless desolation.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2118,'en','This cloak allows you to remain incognito in a cemetery, or to transform yourself at will into a female Chafer. Both these things are entirely useless to anyone but the most criminally perverse among us.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2119,'en','This cloak gives you wings of a sort. The smoke it gives off when you burn it... you''ll be high as a kite.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2154,'en','A ring worn by Silaisie.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2155,'en','An amulet worn by Silaisie.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2156,'en','This sword allows you to preach to the people.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2157,'en','The Clint is a simple but classy hat. The latest version of this hat strangely suits both delicate female adventurers and the more virile male sort. A sure sign of quality, that.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2170,'en','This long sword is heavy and difficult to handle, but it cuts like any sword you can name...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2233,'en','Xof the Fox created this belt after he inexplicably decided to gather up all the teeth he could find on a Wabbit battlefield. It has now become a lifelong passion of his.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2341,'en','Mech Riorraw specially designed this bow. It can cross lava rivers and reach the top of Brakmar walls. No more, no less.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2361,'en','This bow is a creation of the inspired Mulic Bere. Its maximum range is just incredible. The problem is the minimum range can also be as incredible.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2367,'en','Lehunui thought he knew how to make friends. He often invited complete strangers to fancy-dress balls and bought them dinner, champagne and magnificent jewels. His conversation, in contrast, was paltry and extremely monotonous... Most people took the money and ran... stuffing a la carte meals into doggy bags one course after the other to be eaten in better company.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2368,'en','Ramoune was a childhood friend of the sunny Nova. When Ramoune decided to put his spotless mind at rest for an eternal nap, he put an end to their friendship.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2369,'en','This dazzling belt is the result of a mad bet to restore one of the most dazzling belts ever created in Amakna: it''s the Dazzling Belt. Pakape Promethe won the contest.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2370,'en','Some incredibly light equipment that finally brings a little delicacy into the cruel world of the Bwork.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2371,'en','Jiva recommends this belt for those long, cold waking nights. If stained, hand wash with Rimennelle.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2372,'en','Wearing these boots, you''ll feel like you''re walking on fresh grass. Their particular niche is the bio-conservative Hyuppie demographic.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2373,'en','Moon Hair, used to make this pair of boots, is absolutely ideal for keeping your feet warm. These boots are also a heart-warming memory of Moon.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2374,'en','Tarsy the hermit quite obviously couldn''t stand visitors. Any guests who did dare come along quickly left with nothing but a big, red boot mark on their back.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2375,'en','Wearing these boots, you''ll hear the noise of the wind on the coast or the cries of a chafer Lancer lost in the inmost depths of the labyrinth. They''re disturbingly similar.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2376,'en','This axe is the only blade capable of resisting the aggressive power of the Kaerlier tree and therefore, the only one that can cut it down.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2380,'en','It''s a strange cloak made of pieces of Mushd which are very much all of one piece. And you can give the one who is laughing a piece of his mind.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2381,'en','This cloak is made with a pennant, which used to be kept on the highest tower of Amakna Castle. This is probably why it smells like fresh sun-kissed linen waving in a June breeze..');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2382,'en','Maimpa, an Ecaflip who wasn''t afraid of heights... he thought he''d always land on his feet. One day, he landed on a starving Trool and was buried the same day on the very spot where his remains were found... Well, the spot where the biggest pieces were found.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2383,'en','Made of bloody tissue, the Kwag''U Cape feels like stiff cardboard... a bit like a big, cape-shaped scab.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2384,'en','There''s something beastly about these boots. Don''t be shocked if a Boowolf starts humping a limb when you put them on... Does your neck count as a limb? Well, it does for a loved-up Boowolf.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2385,'en','Ideal for laying on the green grass of your garden or wiping the green mess in your nose, the Grazor can is one of the few inanimate objects that can multitask.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2386,'en','This strange cape draws its strength from its rundown look. The dirtier it is, the more useful it is.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2387,'en','This cloak smells very bad - it has to be said. Truth be told, it''s made with a dense mixture of monster hairs, which gives off this wonderful medley of odours.
Do not confuse the Hairy Cloak with Hairy Pie, which is something else entirely.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2388,'en','A long time ago, an Ecaflip follower called Dodge dropped a valuable treasure map which was carved on stone. He made an amulet of the largest piece, believing he would one day unite the pieces once more. Then he lost the amulet.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2389,'en','Dodge brought meaning to his life by smashing, burning, grinding, selling... no, sorry not selling... ehh... throwing away, spitting on... everything he owned. And you should see what he did to his Kamas. My Lord, I know they''re only a moulded piece of copper, but still, I pity those poor coins...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2390,'en','This Amulet is almost perfect. It considerably increases the wisdom of anyone who wears it. It''s useful for making yourself appear wise in front of your friends, or passing yourself off as a model pupil.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2391,'en','There''s an old saying that goes: "Lucky one day, double lucky the day after." The longer you think about it, the more ridiculous that saying gets.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2392,'en','Thanks to the artisans of Amakna who are multitalented, the Modified Dragolyre is almost perfect.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2393,'en','The Osamodas Onehaieuf Bek craved the respect of his guild members, so he decided to create a revolutionary Amulet. He found inspiration one morning while making some breakfast for his friends... Okaaaay!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2394,'en','This heart-warming, sun kissed little thing lends a feeling of invulnerability to the wearer. It''s so light that many wear it for years without realizing they have it on... Yes, there are those among you who do not shower for years at a time.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2395,'en','Mad Bacon was a little vile demon with the enraging habit of standing right in front of people and not moving. He was magic-proof, which imposed a certain respect at the time. The Mad bacon went underground recently, he stood in front of the wrong guy for the wrong length of time.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2396,'en','The name of this amulet is unpronounceable in the language of the country where it is manufactured, for non-natives, anyway. To make it more appealing to the Amaknean market, its designer used the services of a local translator, a certain Lou Gull, to help him come up with a new name. When the designer saw how much Lou Gull charged for his services, he used a cheaper translator instead. Evidently, you get what you pay for.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2397,'en','Law-babe was an old man who took whatever came to hand to create strange, strange items. One day, he made a locket with scrap off the street. He put it round his neck, and felt a strange sensation... a very strange sensation.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2398,'en','The self-made Kaniger Rucky Balboua gave this eye to Melyonen to thank her for introducing his future wife, Adriana, to him. Soon after, they separated. Rucky would scream her name at the top of his voice and burst into tears without the slightest warning.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2399,'en','Barren Sameday, husband to Marman Brigette, was an Ecaflip with extraordinary talents. This Miliboowolf-hair bag containing a lump of bamboo wood was his favourite charm. He''d carve the amount of Kamas he wished to win into the wood with a Kloon Snapper tooth. This gris-gris brought him good and often uncomfortable luck, but above all, incredible wealth.
Maybe he was just good at cards, though.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2400,'en','There''s something... ehh... how shall I put it... dark about these boots. So don''t be surprised if a Vampire falls in love with you when you wear them. I mean I don''t know if you''ve had a hard life up to now, but I would say it would be the worst thing that''s ever happened to you... Like, the worst. Worse than... I dunno. Bad, really. Like, awful.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2402,'en','This sword is only presented to the most accomplished of mercenaries as a kind of conversation piece. That''s not to say a single swipe wouldn''t take your leg off...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2403,'en','In bygone days, it was used for parole, the Peeka Belt has apparently a spare power in relation to the other belts. But nobody has found what it is. You''d better keep a close eye on the thing.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2404,'en','This belt once belonged to a Sewer Rat. It suits it perfectly. What I''m not supposed to tell you is that the little rodent had the most horrifying case of love handle you''ve ever seen.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2409,'en','The Fire Kwak Headdress will make a real charmer out of you... Charm is the second best way of sidelining your enemies in the heat of combat... The other is raw, unpackaged, unapproved-by-the-FDA LUST. Let me tell you, though, with the beasts that wander round these parts, you''ll feel like a big of cheese in a Bonta rat trap if you take the latter approach.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2410,'en','The Treechelmet protects you from hangovers.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2411,'en','This magnificent headgear increases strength and intelligence... if you can stand the smell.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2412,'en','This cloak won''t make you fly but it will itch like hell. Even if you sew a big "S" on it, it won''t work... though some people a few years ago on a cliff were absolutely convinced of it. Too bad.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2413,'en','With these Treechnid Leaves on, you''ll be able to strut about in the forest without being recognized. However, beware of the Treechnids in search of spring buddings.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2414,'en','This cape has it all: it''s hard-wearing, comfortable, colourful and rare... But it smells dreadful, just awful. Well, as we always say, you can''t have it all!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2415,'en','The Fire Kwakblade is a magnificent weapon. Even if you don''t scare your enemy away, at least, you might make an lasting impression.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2416,'en','The user guide explains that this surprising hammer can release astonishingly powerful energy when correctly used. Another Osamodas'' user guide translated into Sadida...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2417,'en','This staff has kept all the aggressiveness of the Treechnid, but hasn''t kept the musty smell which often characterizes old Treechnids.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2418,'en','Using this ring, your master may be able to find you if you get lost while delivering a letter.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2419,'en','This ring once belonged to the renowned Bouze Lite Yeah, the saviour of the modern age. He never stopped going on about some place he used to drink called the Inn ''Finity and Beyond''.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2420,'en','The branch of a Treechnid isn''t easy to carve, but with some perseverance you''ll get a simple and stylish ring. Simple and stylish like a sleeping Osamodas.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2421,'en','With those Fire Kwak spurs on, every Sram for miles around will be on your back.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2422,'en','These are the most comfortable boots ever created. The inside seems to be padded with Gobball Wool and you can feel a liquid running through your toes. For all you know, it could be Gobball Saliva... even Blood. Whatever!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2423,'en','You''d get the same effects out of this pair of Boots as you would from an evening at the tavern. You must have a drink, or plenty of drinks, to get the optimum effect. And the next day, your legs will feel as heavy as these boots.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2424,'en','With all these feathers around your neck, you''ll look like Aldo Rado, the great Sacrier adventurer eternally searching for a golden city.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2425,'en','A fine piece of Gobball horn, this. The material is known for bringing peace and wisdom to these tranquil beasts, so a Gobball amulet should bring peace and wisdom too. Although since you murdered the poor thing to get it, maybe the opposite will happen. Who knows.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2426,'en','This small Arachnee is the proof that you don''t have to stuff an animal to turn it into an amulet. It will tickle your neck and might even spin a web in front of your mouth if you yawn too much or talk too much rubbish.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2427,'en','This Belt is perfect to strut about like a Fire Kwak during the season of love. Provided, of course, that it''s the only thing you''re wearing.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2428,'en','Easy to wear, this belt is quite light in relation to its size. The wool looks brand new... according to the legend, about a hundred Gobballs had to be cut to pieces to get this smooth and silky look.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2429,'en','This belt will increase your self-confidence and give you abs of wood. An anti-Arachnee treatment is nevertheless strongly recommended once a year. It is more or less the same as the hair of a Sadida, but with a lot less anti-parasites.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2435,'en','Thanks to these homemade boots, Kere was the only Eniripsa ever to win the Great Amakna Triathlon. The Ecaflips thought the second coming was at hand when they saw him skimming along on the Asse Sea... For years afterwards he was harassed by Pandawas begging him to turn their water into wine.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2438,'en','The Royal Gobball headgear will never go out of fashion. Besides being elegant, the bearer gains strength and intelligence.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2440,'en','This sword doesn''t know whether it''s coming or going ... It inflicts all types of elemental damage.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2441,'en','This ring increases life, just like the smell of Royal Gobball it gives off increases its charm...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2442,'en','They shine, they radiate power, they are fit for a king! Three cheers.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2443,'en','This amulet increases strength and intelligence');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2444,'en','This magnificent belt increases your vitality and conveniently carries all your items. It''s so soft that you can even use it to bind your lady-love hand and foot when she refuses to stay home.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2445,'en','On top of being classy, this cape, worn by the great Royal Gobball, inspires the wearer with incredible strength.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2446,'en','Without any hairs or threads, this cape remains a mystery for the intellectuals of Amakna. At last count there were ten.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2447,'en','With this headgear on, the hotties will be queuing up to lick you. It''s one of those things Captain Chafer always dreamt of in his own time.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2469,'en','There''s no need to bite your nails with this ring on your fingers, just lick them instead!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2470,'en','These boots are great in summer because they give off a smell of wild strawberries in the heat. Which also masks the smell of perspiration emanating from the hairy toes of an old Sadida.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2471,'en','The worst thing about this item is that when you get hungry, you''ll be tempted to take a bite of it.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2472,'en','This amulet betrays your love of jelly.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2473,'en','Classy but not very effective, this cloak will suit young adventurers nonetheless.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2474,'en','This hat is not really useful for anything... it does scare the boys away quite nicely though...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2475,'en','A small but pleasing ring for beginners which will amuse young children, or Ecaflips.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2476,'en','These standard boots are popular with young folk of adventurous spirit.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2477,'en','A small belt for budding adventurers.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2478,'en','Not too classy or even powerful, but it''s better when you''ve collected the whole set.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2485,'en','The MUST-HAVE item, but only in the North-East of Amakna.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2489,'en','This elegant cape will make you irresistible to all the noobs out there.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2498,'en','The Vegamu attracts swarms of Moskitoes that mistake it for one of their friends. They are always disappointed when they see this character.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2517,'en','This cape used to belong to a famous hero who was famous for confronting the terrible Doctor Wily. This beast wanted to invade and dominate the World of Twelve with his army of summoned creatures. The good Doctor died before his minions had finished eating what he called ''the last supper''.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2518,'en','Silvia sewed this bizarre cape from old curtains. Fortunately, you can''t really tell since it looks more like a mop that''s been boiled in Lousy Pig blood.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2519,'en','This helmet is perfect for excelling in the most extreme situations and the most exclusive company.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2520,'en','This helmet once belonged to the old Jojo, a renowned hero of times gone by. Though he is world-famous for his epic travels, it is still hard to understand the legendary devotion of his fans.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2521,'en','Roll, the boot owner''s lovely sister, specialised in astral taxidermy. Long ago, no one knew the difference between astral taxidermy and regular taxidermy. Nowadays, it''s easy to see that astral taxidermy is the involves stuffing astral creatures. If you still can''t understand where they went wrong, you obviously don''t know just how stupid they were.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2522,'en','These boots enabled the famous Jojo to perfect his famous roundhouse kick, which was known as "Hot Red Kick". No one knows where this name comes from since his boots were unmistakably white!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2523,'en','This belt has been especially designed to protect the hips of our valuable heroes. Totally useless to you then.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2524,'en','Rumour has it that this belt was created by Captain Blooe himself. Isn''t that incredibly... incredible! You do believe me, don''t you?');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2530,'en','A bit heavy but really pretty, you''ll be the queen of the night with these Caraboots on.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2531,'en','Just like you, turtles have very small heads. How convenient! This cap is just the right size for both of you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2532,'en','A practical, well-made cloak. It won''t make a champion out of you, but then again, I can''t think of anything that would make a champion out of you...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2534,'en','Ideal for keeping cool in those hot summers on Moon Island, as well as ideal to cool down the advances of your more eager paramours, this cape will satisfy all the needs of the modern adventurer.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2535,'en','This Ice Kwak headdress will keep your head full of fresh and brilliant ideas. And before you say anything, it doesn''t work on Iops.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2537,'en','Ideal for toning your hips, this belt will allow you to keep cool below the belt too.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2544,'en','Dreadfully sharp and incredibly classy, this blade will make your Crow friends jealous.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2545,'en','With these boots you''ll feel incredibly light and peculiarly ridiculous.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2546,'en','Thanks to this magnificent helmet, you''ll have all the class of the notorious Lord Crow.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2547,'en','Long ago, the best Tailors of Amakna united to scavenge the remains of Lord Crow and make the greatest cloak the world has ever seen. It looks incredible draped grandly over your shoulders, but for some reason, it gives you the strong urge to eat cheese.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2587,'en','This Hatchet is the ideal mascot for any lumberjack. It''s not really useful (you can''t fell a tree with it), but having it attached to your belt might calm and reassure you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2589,'en','This small Axe can''t cut down trees but can protect you against small monsters. If you find yourself face to face with a Minotoror, just drop it and run.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2590,'en','One day, a Bwork smith apprentice made a range of axes, a range of one size fits all, ergonomic, axes... THE ideal weapon for a young, simple-minded adventurer like yourself.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2592,'en','Very light and easy to handle, this axe allows the Bambou chopper to keep well out of harm''s way.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2593,'en','This axe, made of Oliviolet wood, is the only one that can harm the Oliviolet. You gotta fight fire with fire.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2595,'en','This axe might be primitive, but it''s also very deadly... a like a kick between the legs.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2597,'en','This long axe worms its way into the cracks of the biggest trees and splits the giants in half. It''s use in battle is no different. Ouch!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2600,'en','This big axe makes a horrendous noise when it falls on something, reducing everyone in the vicinity to petrified silence.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2601,'en','Darsson was a valiant Enutrof, though he was not very good with his hands. As he often dropped his shovel in fights, he decided to tie a spare axe onto his belt. It saved his life more than once. Then he dropped his axe. Poor bugger will never have kids.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2603,'en','This axe is very useful for chopping up the more stubborn parts of a tree, such as the grizzled knots on an old oak... A few swipes with this fellow and you''ll have a perfectly round trunk.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2604,'en','This bardiche is mainly employed by the militiamen of Amakna. Its unusually large size and girth undoubtedly compensate for something else.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2606,'en','Many inscriptions can be read on this big Hatchet. Its creator, Claus Ansipedi, thought it would be a good idea to bring a semblance of culture to those cretinous dogs. What a waste of time! Just as he was about to finish his inscriptions, a crazed Amaknan drunk cracked the poor man''s skull open for ''spoiling a perfectly good axe.''');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2608,'en','This axe was forged between two great stones, and changed hands so many times in the process that it has travelled the world ten times over in its lifetime.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2612,'en','This long axe is used by horny-fisted seamen to battle the biggest fish the briny depths vomit to the surface. It will atomize anything smaller than a whale.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2614,'en','Dame Zel was a pretty young princess who radiated intelligence and freshness. During a Bwork raid on her city, she shocked everyone when she took out this axe and, Moses-like, sent half the besieging army to oblivion.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2615,'en','This axe is well known for rapidly and permanently resolving disputes between drunken Enutrofs.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2616,'en','This axe owes its name to the test made to prove its dreadful efficiency: a gigantic axe, a mythophobiac and a hall full of bards.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2629,'en','This cape, which looks royal, offers incredible protection. It made the reputation of a renowned female tailor who died victim of her success, squashed in the crowd.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2637,'en','This curved blade, made of bone, horn and cartilage is as sharp as an Ecaflip''s claw.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2638,'en','100% natural, this sword was forged from the sixth claw of an Ecaflip. Don''t go picking your nose with it!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2639,'en','A female Ecaflip smith created this sword after failing to master the ancestral technique "Ceangal Claw". She called her sword "Fake Ceangal Claw", happy in the knowledge she could master something at last.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2640,'en','Strangely sculpted, this staff doesn''t come from around here. It smells a lot like a dark, dank corner of Brakmar.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2641,'en','This hat comes in red and white and is so classy, you''ll be invited to all the best parties in town. If you see the Ambassador, as you soon surely will, don''t forget to thank him in the traditional way: "Ambassador, you''re really spoiling us with these..."');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2655,'en','This belt is a patchwork of Lord Crow''s body parts. Once equipped with it, you''ll have a wonderful sensation of power. LeChouque even agreed to add his buckle as a show of support.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2677,'en','This belt has been made out of LeChouque''s most powerful belongings, notably his famous boxer shorts. It''s enough to plunge the entire female clientele of the Pirates Bar into mass confusion.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2678,'en','This belt almost looks like a loincloth. Very convenient for camouflaging yourself among the Kokokos of Moon Island, or even seducing one of them.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2681,'en','This small belt is ideal for protecting your most sensitive parts from critical blows. 
Just check that the shoemaker has removed the owner from the shell before trying it.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2683,'en','This small belt is ideal for protecting your most sensitive parts from critical blows. 
Just check that the shoemaker has removed the owner from the shell before trying it.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2685,'en','This small belt is ideal for protecting your most sensitive parts from critical blows. 
Just check that the shoemaker has removed the owner from the shell before trying it.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2687,'en','This small belt is ideal for protecting your most sensitive parts from critical blows. 
Just check that the shoemaker has removed the owner from the shell before trying it.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2688,'en','Once you have equipped this belt it''s hard to lose it, that''s the least you can say! The scatterbrains and the serial victims of theft among you will be grateful.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2689,'en','The shoemaker who created this belt using the leftovers of a Dragoturkey, certainly didn''t think too hard about the name.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2710,'en','An improved model of the standard version, the Wild Banisation Belt has been specially reinforced with hunting Wild Dragoturkeys in mind.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2803,'en','That strange belt is made entirely of fragments of crab claws and shells. Even with its powerful magic, it will smell of fish forever and ever, you''d just better get used to it.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2804,'en','The Boowolf donated his precious organs for the making of this incredible belt. Not willingly of course, but we can still be thankful. Don''t trust its strange appearance, which could unnerve the most depraved Chafer - it''s very powerful.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2807,'en','Bowisse the Shoemaker made this belt. He gave it to Brouce Boulgoure when the legendary lumberjack managed to uproot the Soft Oak... You don''t even deserve to hear about such heroism, child!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2808,'en','Yes my child, it will be hard to resist you with this belt on. Bowisse consequently advises you to never get too close to a Dragon Pig while wearing it. They''re known to be lusty devils.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2809,'en','Behind the grotesque name, hides a beautiful creation by Bowisse the Shoemaker. Behind the beautiful creation, hides a grotesque reality... the belt is made of the skin and bones of Bowisse''s Chafer victims.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2810,'en','The magical powers of this magnificent red belt will help you concentrate better and learn quicker. Some Iops even manage to hobble to the end of the alphabet before their ignorant lives are extinguished.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(2811,'en','Here''s a belt that''ll please the thrill-seekers among you! It was designed to aid the easy and safe hunting of Ouginaks. Mortality rates remained the same as before, but hunters kept wearing the thing. You have to admit it''s classy though, no?');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(3203,'en','The supposed origin of this ring is doubtful, to say the least. Apparently it once belonged to a clan of Kanniballs of the worst type, the fern eaters. Certainly a story to frighten any young Sadida, and quite a few older Sadidas too.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(3204,'en','As of last spring, this is officially the trendiest belt on the streets of Bonta. The insignia of a renowned brotherhood of shoemakers adorns the buckle.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(3205,'en','It''s the most fashionable belt in the sewers of Brakmar, perfect if you''re looking to give the impression that you''re a hard nut to crack. In your case it''s just an impression, but it''s useful nonetheless.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(3206,'en','Specially designed to reward skilful knights, the Xerbo must be worn without underwear and in winter only.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(3207,'en','These boots are a dramatic improvement on even the most carefully crafted footwear. Comfortable and light, they promise consistent pedal satisfaction with every wear. At the sight of this pair, even your opponent will give a faintly happy, wistfully envious smile.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(3356,'en','Some people may laugh at you because of this surprising shovel but what does it matter? It''s time to accept your style and your personal taste!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(3357,'en','In Amakna, when pupils are too loud, too quiet, too smart or too dumb, they receive a firm smash on the knuckles with this hammer. Iop teachers in particular find it works wonders in the context of their one-tiered educational system.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(3647,'en','This sickle-like dagger was used to gut travellers who lost their way. It owes its name to the numerous binge drinking parties the owner organised with the money stolen from his victims. More specifically, the name refers to the morning after.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(3648,'en','Captain Chafer has disappeared but you have his dagger in your hands. Just imagine what the blade must have seen all that time it was in his murderous grasp.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(3649,'en','We owe this magnificent blade to a craftsman named Daguiero. Before a descent into gambling and other dubious activities, this was his last creation worthy of interest. Not a bad way of ending a career...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(3650,'en','These powerful daggers are the result of a collaboration between a group of wise craftsmen in order to secure their professional future. The group consisted of two. They both died arguing over the name of the daggers.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(3651,'en','A ridiculous, pint-sized artisan named Slaillehine had the wonderful notion of making these magnificent daggers.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(3652,'en','Marie Aigue knew how to treat the men folk. With her big staff, she thwarted the advances of many a great Iop knight. One fine day, it was discovered that Marie Aigue was, in fact, a boy dressed as a girl. Suddenly it all made sense.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(4241,'en','This fantastic colours of this sword will pierce right to your enemy''s heart... Then you can cut it out carefully! Exactly what an Ecaflipette would do! The magnificent colour is obtained by soaking the blade in monsters'' entrails for several centuries.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(4242,'en','This sword was originally an ornate fan for overheated ladies. All you had to do was wave it energetically about the face. The product was soon withdrawn when angry widowers complained they couldn''t put their wives'' heads back on. It was quickly re-launched as a lethal weapon. That''s market research for you!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(4381,'en','This strange amulet allows its wearer to relax, chill out and have a nap, right in the middle of a fight. Just like a Feca, in fact.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(4382,'en','This sword, with its cold, sharp blade makes the most primitive instincts bubble to the top. Each gesture, even with the best of intentions, results in a blow below the belt.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(4684,'en','This amulet contains a part of the Plain Crackler''s story that could be summed-up in two lines if anyone knew it. Unfortunately, even the Cracklers have forgotten how it goes...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(5122,'en','Epuop Tik himself ordered this amulet from a renowned jeweller. He wanted to play with several dolls at the same time instead of having to wait for the death of one doll before summoning a new one. It''s quite common practice among Sadidas.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(5999,'en','This wand gets its frightening powers from its creation, in conditions identical to those at the centre of the earth. That''s the story anyway, but try to find someone with a bit of proof...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6438,'en','This Wand is composed of soft materials, making it very tricky to use. However, once produced in combat by an experienced warrior, it reveals its true power.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6439,'en','This ethereal wand is the result of a magic mixture of supernatural elements. Sometimes frightening, sometimes whacky, this wand is the epitome of instability.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6440,'en','This wand is not just an ordinary ball of hair. Its centre absorbs the magic essence of the tufts that fall on it and merges them all together as long hairball. As strange as it may seem, it works!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6442,'en','Always looking for ways to surprise his enemies, the Sadida Aga Dou took care to hang a small doll at the sharp end of his staff. Young Iopettes inevitably rush towards it to get the doll and die from severe impalement.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6443,'en','The renowned and hilarious Yamato, a craftsman unjustly despised because of his ridiculous bow, was the first to dare to imbue an amulet with magic... until then it was believed to be impossible.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6444,'en','Apart from its colour, this amulet has no connection whatsoever to the famous Turquoise Dofus. However, it is every bit as powerful. Sometimes you can read a book by its cover...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6445,'en','This bow has been crafted with the utmost care, giving it a perfect curvature. It is said that its creator used the buttocks of a female Gobball as a model. Tragically, she was cut in half when the bow maker accidentally strung the bow with her inside.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6446,'en','Chiduc was a Bow Carver, renowned for his errors of pronunciation. He was incapable of pronouncing the letter "b" without adding an "ow" behind. Yet another indication of his erratic genius.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6449,'en','Personally I can''t think of a better way of impressing the girls at the bus stop than turning yourself into a shadow or even into Lord Crow. This cape will let you to do just that. It also makes a great pillow... if you''re lucky.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6450,'en','Aman, a renowned female shoemaker had a lover who often stood her up. As love is blind, she still gave him this magnificent belt as a symbol of their secret love.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6451,'en','Seeing this bow, you have to wonder why it has such a soppy name. Maybe it''s a respectful prayer to its hordes of victims.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6452,'en','This strangely-shaped bow is a work of art. The Bow Sculptor who created it is also renowned for having exhibited his most controversial models in Loopine''s cave, a place forbidden to all but the most hedonistic of bohemians.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6453,'en','This weapon was inspired by this ancient, incredibly specific, Chinese axiom: "Many''s the bow that was useful for catching a flying fish and then cooking it on a slow barbeque for several minutes each side, being particularly handy for turning said fish or plucking it out of the coals should it take a tumble."');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6454,'en','This Dark Treechnid branch is in fact one of the creature''s arms. Ideal for arm-wrestling training, it''s above all an excellent weapon for terrorizing your childhood enemies or torturing the Trunknids.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6459,'en','Your only chance to survive in a mine infested with dark miners is to have light. Since you''ll never manage to steal one of their precious candles, just wear this amulet... at least it''ll bring you some luck.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6460,'en','This magnificent brooch pays homage to the resistance of the miners of the Grimoth Silver Mine. They spent a winter fighting a Crackler of the worst kind but in the end they were killed by a Tofu who wandered into their hideout on his way home. Boy isn''t life unfair.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6461,'en','It was this Amulet, which was especially designed for older Enutrofs, that allowed Setag get rid of all the other miners in the Grimoth mine. Quite heavy-handed, but very effective, it must be said.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6462,'en','This little brooch is truly lovely. It was made to encourage unlucky people to try their luck at the fun fair, but it''s also useful when you go on epic hunting expeditions.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6463,'en','This ring was made by a famous oriental itinerant, but unfortunately no one could remember his name. He died during an archery contest, putting a Wild Sunflower seed on his head instead of the larger Pumpkin variety.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6464,'en','This ring is an improved version of the celebrated Ring of Satisfaction. It''s ideal if you want to step out of the blood-red spotlight of dangerous battle.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6465,'en','Loopine once asked the monster that haunted his cave the secret to making this ring. The monster said he''d have to do him a few favours in return, and Loopine gladly agreed.  
Let''s just say the poor guy never wanted to see another ring in his life after the monster was finished with him, let alone make the bloody things. Blimey!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6466,'en','This amulet allowed Shika Ingalsse to survive on several occasions when furious Gobballs, bent on making her life a misery, attacked her.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6467,'en','Nobody knows who the owner of this ring is. He wanted to remain anonymous after a humiliating defeat inflicted by a summoned Arachnee. We must say in his defence that this Arachnee had been compelled by a Iop...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6468,'en','While other Iops of his age got presents like a Tabi or a wooden Goultard for their communion, Vald got this ring. It''s hardly something you can show off to your friends but it''s very useful for fighting.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6469,'en','This wedding ring has been worn down by the scratching of barley through hundreds of harvests. It was even there to witness the union of Farle and Shika when they got married in the middle of barley field one spring!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6470,'en','These magnificent boots are perfect for kicking Gobballs in the arse when you''re herding the difficult little runts. Children respond just as well to the same encouragement.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6471,'en','These small shoes have been reinforced, repaired and deodorized. They are often used to trap Mush-Mush since the substratum left out by the Lousy Pig seems appetizing to them...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6472,'en','This padded Golden Dreggon Shell will protect you from bolts of Bwork Magus lightning. Sadly, it won''t protect you from real lightning strikes, or the angry, baying mob complaining how, in the good old days of Old Amaknean, lightning strikes used to be called ''strikings''.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6473,'en','This shell of Sapphire Dreggon will suit you perfectly. Not everyone is made for it, though... just take a look at the Iops... the bloody idiots don''t even wear it the right way round!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6474,'en','This Black Dreggon shell is ideal if you want to remain discreet by night, and is thus quite popular with two deeply divergent sections of society: peeping Toms in the port of Madrestam and those gentle souls, the Piwi watchers of Amakna. The annual convention is always a hoot, a real hoot.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6477,'en','This magnificent hat will help you see everything as bright as daylight, especially during the daytime. It can also be useful to dazzle the beasts haunting the mines or to make Iops believe you''re... well anything you tell them.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6481,'en','This magnificent hat was created on Dora Bora Island, south of Moon Island. Perfectly adapted to fight, it''s also much appreciated as a fruit basket, for traumatised Kokokos nuts for instance.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6482,'en','An improved version of the Jouik Kramp, this hat was made out of the best resources found on Moon Island, giving it a rural character. Even if you don''t look like a Kanniball, you''ll still give some great headbutts.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6483,'en','According to the legend, this impressive helmet turns anyone who wears it into a Bronze Bwork. The helmet was held responsible for a string of incidents where defenceless hobos mysteriously disappeared, leaving only the taste of licked spoon behind them.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6484,'en','When daggers are not enough anymore, when gods are making fun of you, you have to find your own way of fighting. Some followers of Sram have apparently understood, others are still counting on the help of gods...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6485,'en','Because of his clattering bones and an obvious lack of dexterity and intelligence, Archer Chafer has never been able to handle such a bow as this one. Although your bones may not shake like his, there''s no guarantee a beginner like yourself won''t look just as foolish.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6491,'en','This bow is a messed up crossbreed of a Trunknid and a Treechnid. It''s obviously a failure for a Lumberjack, but a true success for a Bow Carver. Your parents wish they could say the same about you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6492,'en','The distance between the two ends of this staff is identical to the space between the eyes of the Lenalds... Will these howwible Wabbits stop at nothing?');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6493,'en','These wabbits thongs give you the "cawwot attitude." They are recommended by experts of ritual dancing, tap-dancing or the Captain Chafer fast tango.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6494,'en','Used by the most renowned Amaknan Eniripsas, this wand is a great for casting vicious spells at your enemies. Most people use it to make themselves or their friends more intelligent. They say... though I find it hard to believe myself... but they say that someone once turned a Iop into a rat with this. Such an enormous leap in intelligence is unlikely, but try it out!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6495,'en','Made from the remains of the Soft Oak, this wand is ultra-powerful. Just wave it from right to left according to the specified patterns and it may trigger a shower of toads... or you may look like a perfect idiot.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6496,'en','This wand can sometimes turn against its owner. In this case, the best thing you can do is to give it to one of your enemies, or to a Iop - idiots like them will certainly believe it''s a present.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6497,'en','Brouce Boulgoure''s wife, an Eniripsa, always stole her husband''s famous axe. To stop her, he cut off one of her wings and an arm. Then, when he inevitably regretted it, he gave her this wand. What a gentleman.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6498,'en','These briefs of respectable size still sport the marks of their former owner (plus some really strange hairs). On the buttocks or on the head, this garment will bring you unlimited respect around Amakna.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6499,'en','The teeth of this amulet have eaten away more Cawwots than Brouce Boulgoure has uprooted trees, so don''t be surprised if you find Tiwabbits trying to give you kisses on the neck as a result of your powerful Cawwot awoma.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6500,'en','These Ears won''t improve your hearing but the good news is that your friends will easily spot you in a crowd...and that your enemies will have a good laugh. Keep smiling, this pair of ears will prove essential with time.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6501,'en','If you carry this bag on your back, you can go on a trip without worrying about food. Even if the Cawwot is as empty as a Iop''s skull, the leaves on top of it can grow again. Ideal to make herbal tea.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6503,'en','The Polpullet is the result of a cross breed between an aggressive Fire Kwak and a sickly Tofu. Time out of mind, the Polpullet hunt has been an unchanged ritual. Hunting this horrible creature is a pleasure on many levels.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6504,'en','The only things we know about the creator of this hammer are his nickname - a certain Fantal - and his woeful taste. He loved covering himself with Royal Jelly and Tofu feathers... An expensive, useless activity. Some people are starving for God''s sake.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6505,'en','This Hammer is ideal for fighting horned beasts... It isn''t recommended you nail your colours to the mast with it, though...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6506,'en','An Enutrof legend says that a miner is "gogorified" when he can''t stand daylight anymore, a result of spending so much time working down his mine. Never bring a candle close to such a miner, he could turn you into bronze.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6507,'en','The Terps was a very nasty creature, as dangerous and hated as the old Liche, its great rival. Determined to surpass its nemesis, the Terps created this hammer to crush its toes but ended up destroying its feet. The beginning of a great love story.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6508,'en','An exceptional hammer which is ideal to take care either of your darling little Prespic or of your enemies if you''re a follower of Chafer Fu.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6509,'en','This magnificent hammer turned the heads of many an Osamodas. It''s so impressive that people still turn around when they pass by its bearer. You wouldn''t believe the number of chronic neck injuries this bloody thing has caused.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6510,'en','Kahr was mad for hammer fighting, always fighting with that hammer he was. His pet name for it was ''Quire Boy'', since, like many a 12th century singer, this hammer never did see a nail.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6511,'en','It''s the perfect hammer for talking yourself out of sticky situations. You''ll be an instant success at all the best parties too. Just don''t abuse its power. Yeah, you know what I mean.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6512,'en','It''s THE weapon Xelors dreamt of when they were fifteen, especially those looking for thrills and spills. It helps them to get over the endemic Xelor height complex nicely.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6513,'en','This hammer''s power comes from a subtle enchantment. You can''t see it at first sight, nor at second. I thought it was worth pointing it out to increase its value for naive buyers.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6516,'en','A Sram would cut his own parents up if you gave him these daggers at the wrong moment. They cannot resist. Some say they were invented by a powerful group of anti-Sramites who gleefully watch the entire population wipe itself out one by one.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6517,'en','Any Srams looking for a new experience would be well advised to get their hands on a pair of these daggers. Their strange powers fill them with treacherous potential... for enemies or friends. The Captain Chafer would have loved them.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6518,'en','Made by a famous sculptor, this wand has won the great N''hi Wand competition no less than 13 times. It easily beat old Boulgourde models, which were later taken off the market... too dangerous to be used by young Eniripsas.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6519,'en','A renowned carver, he changed his name when he started using metal in his creations. Unfortunately, vanity often accompanies genius.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6520,'en','The sculptor of this wand tried many times to change the unfortunate name of his magical weapon, but sales always plummeted. Any publicity is good publicity.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6521,'en','People say that this staff would make a female Treechnid blush. We would not recommend you make use of this feature, male Treechnids are very possessive creatures...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6522,'en','People say this root is herbivorous. It quickly worms its way through dead leaves and eats young shoots. Very impressive. But, well, unless you''re fighting Dandelions, it''s completely useless.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6523,'en','This very stylish carved root will make an experienced summoner of you. Nothing to write home about in itself, but it''s a magnet for the female Sadidas.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6524,'en','A shy old Sadida tried to lure a young, beautiful female into Hornbeam Wood with this root. He waited for one hundred years but she stood him up. Since that day, walking past some Savage Root on your way to a date is considered a very bad omen.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6525,'en','The inhabitants of Amakna were fed up of hearing Fecas constantly complaining about their spells, so they made this staff to give them something else to moan about. Blah blah blah, bring 2-turn Immunity back, blah blah blah. Give it a rest, already!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6526,'en','The smith who created this shovel wanted to stay anonymous, as a mark of modesty. But he left a clue in the name of the shovel that would lead devotees of his work to his real identity. These craftsmen are vain after all...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6527,'en','Krys Mass was an illustrious Shovel Smith. He was always singing about shovels, out loud and out of tune. This scarred his wife for good, and she transferred the wounds onto the shovel she made him.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6528,'en','This Shovel has explored all the continents, watched the sun set on the ridge of Crackler Mountain and rise over the tranquil Asse Sea. What? You''ve never gone further than Moon Island? Shame on you!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6535,'en','This strange multi-purpose shovel was used to kill lice, to remove dandruff and to get Iops to learn their nine times tables.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6536,'en','Dark Miners use this shovel, which is as large as the hand of a Crackler, to crush several Eniripsas at once. Try doing the same, you''ll feel great.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6537,'en','This shovel is really obnoxious. Nobody knows why, but the Mairhes Shovels are always unbearably cheeky. They must have some good qualities... everyone does for god''s sake...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6538,'en','This shovel allows the Enutrofs to see far into the distance... It''s not magic or anything, they just stick it in the ground and climb onto it. Ideal for finding your house when you''re lost in a field of gigantic ferns.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6539,'en','This shovel is really different from the others. People will make fun of you if you use it during a fight. One-liner jokes about the Gicque Shovel are really popular at the Inn. I find that kind of humour gross and offensive, but you''ll probably laugh your thick skull off...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6540,'en','People say the creator of this shovel truly resembled a beast. A kind of mix between a Boowolf and a Sadida. His shovel is said to have fallen in love with him. What a load of nonsense.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6604,'en','Beyond the realms of the Tofu, the Gobball and even the Iop, there is a creature dwelling in a dimension of idiocy unimaginable even to your cretinous mind: the Quaquack!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6642,'en','This sword is only presented to the most accomplished of mercenaries as a kind of conversation piece. That''s not to say a single swipe wouldn''t take your leg off...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6654,'en','Just listen to this... the Sewer Warden was devoured by the female Sewer Warden. He was digested for more than 100 years before he finally died. His boots were fortunately more resistant than he was and they are still in good condition.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6660,'en','You''ll be irresistible with this hat. You''ll break hearts and discover the true meaning of Glory!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6662,'en','This wonderful 100% southern larva silk hat, washable in fresh water, will make your beloved melt like a Mint Jelly in the sun.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6663,'en','With this wonderful bouquet of Demonic Roses, you will show your beloved you''re ready to brave a thousand and one dangers for her/his sweet little face. For a modest sum and without a sore.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6676,'en','This sword is only presented to the most accomplished of mercenaries as a kind of conversation piece. That''s not to say a single swipe wouldn''t take your leg off...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6677,'en','This sword is only presented to the most accomplished of mercenaries as a kind of conversation piece. That''s not to say a single swipe wouldn''t take your leg off...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6707,'en','This stench-soaked cloak is made from pus-impregnated Mummy Nova Bandages. Enough to have the inhabitants of cemeteries for miles around turned on in their graves.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6712,'en','This magnificent cape smells like fruits of the forest. Not enough to drive a Craette mad about you, but enough to drown the stink of a sloppy Sadida.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6713,'en','Soaked with the blood of the terrible Lordsoth, these daggers helped him bring down the Chafer King during the famous dagger throwing contest at Troolmusement park. The Chafer King never again revealed his leather briefs and went into exile with the illustrious Captain Chafer in the surroundings of the Pandala cemetery.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6716,'en','This pinchy little monkey seems to like you now. It''s very docile but it has a huge appetite. It''ll only eat things that are native to its own island.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000057,'en','This pinchy little monkey seems to like you now. It''s very docile but it has a huge appetite. It''ll only eat things that are native to its own island.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6717,'en','Take this dog to the park, take him to the toilet, show him to your friends, but whatever you do - and please listen carefully - do not feed him. This pet will remove your arm up to the elbow. 
(THIS LEGENDARY PET DOESN''T NEED TO EAT)');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6718,'en','The fairer sex of the fairest class will fall under the spell of this cuddly little ball of fluff. For this reason alone it''s to be avoided.
(THIS LEGENDARY PET DOESN''T NEED TO EAT)');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6719,'en','This strange headgear used to belong to the notorious Bearman. Sewn from the remains of the head of a decomposing bear, the headgear will itself turn heads thanks to the unmistakable whiff-trace that follows you wherever you go.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6720,'en','This beautiful cloak has been worn for years by the famous Bearman. It won''t turn you into a bear, but you will be able to rival the greatest of fighters.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6721,'en','These boots are lined with bear fur: even the coldest-blooded creatures will have toasty warm feet.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6722,'en','The Bearman has vowed never to take off this wedding ring in memory of his dead wife... the besotted groom summoned a bear to impress his newly-wed love. She went to give it a hug... the summoned bear, raised by a distant father and an abusive mother, thought she was trying to beat him... you can guess the rest... The most tragic thing about this story is that Bearman hadn''t made a single payment on the ring. Man, that has to hurt!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6723,'en','The Bearman was wearing this necklace around his neck when he faced the hooligans of Bimdhul''s lair. Legend has it that the amulet saved him, but on close inspection, you can see why it''s just a legend.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6724,'en','This little bear hair-covered belt will hide your love handles perfectly. You should wear it always to avoid disappointing your spectators.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6725,'en','The Bearman used this staff to tame his summoned Bear and from time to time, to rap his children''s knuckles when they didn''t do their homework. Here''s a man who understood the value of education.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6731,'en','With this amulet around your neck, you might fool yourself into thinking people won''t smell your breath. No chance!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6732,'en','Long ago this small ring was much sought after by Enutrofettes who preferred to use it to decorate their toes. An excellent way of hiding their warts.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6742,'en','This amulet is made of a mixture of Ambusher leaves and litter from Moon island. It looks more like a garland than a real amulet, but it will help you seduce the wildlife of the island, which almost exclusively consists of abominable creatures. No Ambusher will resist you, they all will fly into your arms to give you a hickey. Only the most unlucky in love will appreciate this piece.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6743,'en','Take some Ambusher leaves, pile them up, let them macerate in stale alcohol, pierce them, drink the left-over alcohol, stick the leaves around a piece of bark, fix some pieces of Kokoko leaves with a slimy material, and here is a magnificent Deceitful Wedding Ring. It smells really bad and it will be quite handy for you to justify the smell of your fingers overall if you have a tendency to put them everywhere. Especially where you shouldn''t.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6744,'en','Once you''ve tried these boots on, you won''t be able to part with them. Not because they are exceptional, but because they are exceptionally sticky. A feature they often share with female Ambushers...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6745,'en','Outstanding handicraft made of remains of Ambushers and litter picked up along the Moon beaches, in the middle of the foul foam, this belt, when worn alone, will give you a really surprising look. Enough to disconcert your enemies or surprise your beloved, you''ll be able to take advantage of this special moment when, for once, you''ll have the upper hand.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6746,'en','Oto Mustam, the leader of the Brakmar warriors, wore this small amulet long ago... though only at the organised orgies of Brakmar. They say it doubled as a leash!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6747,'en','When the wind blows in its feathers, the Wind Kwak feels as free as an eagle, gliding like a dead leaf carried by a gust of wind. In spite of the clumsy description, it really is quite impressive.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6748,'en','Judiciously worn, this ring will make your stubby little fingers look a little longer. Unfortunately for some, it only works on fingers.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6749,'en','This ring is so light that it could be blown off by the least gust of wind. But don''t expect you''ll be taken away with it. At best, you''ll be safe, humiliated and on solid ground.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6750,'en','Cold and sharp, this blade will revive its users'' most primitive instincts.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6751,'en','"This ribbed blade is lubricated for increased pain." That''s what the handbook says... What is that supposed to mean?');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6752,'en','Ideal for cutting clouds, this blade will also dissect Moskitoes and split hairs.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6753,'en','As perfect as ice-skates on frozen lakes, these boots are very useful for keeping your feet cool, or storing your flask. Recommendations? Don''t put them by the fire to dry, you''ll never see them again.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6754,'en','"Nothing''s better for the feet than a pair of Earth Kwakoboots" said Rola Ingalsse, the famous ploughwoman. Soon after she somehow shovelled a giant clod of earth into her own eyes and was blind for ever more.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6755,'en','Basic but efficient, these surprisingly light boots are sometimes used as wind socks. Listen carefully though... People who find themselves downwind of this improvised apparatus often die.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6756,'en','Ideal for camouflaging yourself as a lump of earth, this cloak will help you attack ploughmen by surprise and steal their treasures. It is for this reason that collectors of ancient pottery covet it so fiercely.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6757,'en','Light and refined, this creation is also used as a curtain by the most destitute in the region. Mummy Nova herself used to wear this as an evening dress.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6758,'en','The Earth Kwak is not very social and is especially hunted for its feathers, as everybody knows. If you wear this belt around your hips, you''ll have the Earth Kwak hunters thinking you''re an over the hill Kwak. Sometimes appearances can be truer than reality.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6759,'en','"The only way to catch an upset old male Wind Kwak is to dress up as an upset female Wind Kwak. Then, the male will try to understand why the female is upset and will try every possible means to satisfy her. Once the male is satisfied with his performance, you should take advantage of his beatitude to fleece him." This is what one can read in part twelve of book three on Wind Kwak hunting. Besides, it is clearly specified that this belt is an essential element to pass yourself off as a female Wind Kwak. You know what you have to do now.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6760,'en','This Earth Kwak headdress is so heavy it''ll always keep your feet on the ground. If the ground happens to be soft, well, it''ll keep your chin on the ground.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6761,'en','To keep your hair streaming in the wind even with a headdress, there''s nothing like this lovely Wind Kwak Headdress which will certainly enable you to give free rein to your hair in most circumstances. It is enough to take the most blasé of Chafers aback.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6762,'en','"For a punch-up, there''s nothing like an Ambusher-up." This is what could be read on the A-Team Travel Agency''s advertising leaflet. The agency offered to rebuild this staff for their clients themselves from various resources scattered on Moon Island. Some sort of treasure hunt except there are no maps.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6763,'en','As the story goes, the dead Ambushers are very comfortable once they have taken the time to rot under the sun. Indeed, they become much more flexible and softer with time. Many adventurers would like to say the same about their beloved.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6764,'en','This headgear isn''t giving you the smartest look, is it? But you do still look less stupid with it on. So just keep it!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6766,'en','This apparently simple amulet was made from three magic ears of Corn, covered with the dust of precious stones, and planted in the Snossios plains during the thirteenth harvest of Istrabraq. It gives incredible courage to its bearer, who with its help can reap entire plains and valleys without rest.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6767,'en','Shika covered this bracelet of precious stones with a hempen cloth to avoid drawing the Crows'' attention while Farle sowed his barley.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6769,'en','This magnificent staff has very beautiful teeth on one end, which makes for an excellent fork. Farle used it to make huge haystacks - higher than the biggest Elm growing in the Eltneg forest of old. It is said that Brouce Boulgoure himself felled the tree for this staff, in return for an unbelievable quantity of oat flakes, which Shika Ingalsse himself offered. He used to gulp down fistfuls before spending days on end hacking entire phyla out of existence.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6771,'en','This ring hasn''t proved itself yet. It is a unique creation made by a jeweller''s apprentice for an important test. It is made from a standard iron ring plunged into a magic Tea solution.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6773,'en','This amulet was made in the Tude manner, hence its name. It is one of the earliest and simplest forms of jewellery, and so it is used to train apprentice jewellers. It is true that the thing is not very powerful, but you can''t have it all, can you?');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6774,'en','These hooves have been carved from various rare woods, reinforced with leather pieces of priceless value and padded with magic cereals. Light, stylish and comfortable, these hooves will resist the passage of time. Many misogynistic adventurers would like to say the same about their beloved.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6775,'en','This cape, a fashionable patchwork of cloth and leather, has allowed Farle Ingalsse to single-handedly sow entire fields for numberless seasons on end. Once folded up and used as a pouch, its capacity seems to be almost unlimited. Nobody really knows the tailor behind this marvel. All the story tells us is that his business went tail-up when his clients began to confuse his cloaks with floor cloths. What a sad end to a fine career!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6776,'en','This belt served Farle Ingalsse as a butcher''s apron when slaughtering Gobballs in his makeshift abattoir. A cruel, thankless task which he nevertheless carried out with obvious and undignified pleasure.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6778,'en','This straw hat has been made with several plaited magic ears, and padded on the inside with various types of hair and fabrics hand sewn by Farle''s wife, Shika Ingalsse. Classier than the Ninnish, and more stylish than the Doddgy, this hat will protect you from the heat as it did Farle through hundreds of long harvests. In this hat, you''ll own those fields.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6780,'en','With this basic-looking weapon, you''ll feel like you know how to fight.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6781,'en','With this basic-looking weapon, you''ll feel like you know how to fight.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6782,'en','With this basic-looking weapon, you''ll feel like you know how to fight.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6783,'en','With this basic-looking weapon, you''ll feel like you know how to fight.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6784,'en','With this basic-looking weapon, you''ll feel like you know how to fight.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6785,'en','With this basic-looking weapon, you''ll feel like you know how to fight.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6786,'en','With this basic-looking weapon, you''ll feel like you know how to fight.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6789,'en','This small amulet blooms in spring, dries out in summer, fades in autumn, and goes rotten in winter. An ideal opportunity to change your style with the passing seasons.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6791,'en','With this little ring on your finger, you''ll be able to walk through fields in the countryside. What do you mean you can do that already? Wow!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6792,'en','This deflower-shaped staff is made from the remains of wild flowers that were cut down in cruel and bloody battles. All the anger and hatred felt by the poor flowers is concentrated in this tiny tool. This weapon is used by the most treacherous Srams who lure naive females with their ''bunch of deflowers''...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6793,'en','This ring has proven its worth, as shown by the little mark made on the inside. It is a unique creation made by a jeweller apprentice for an important test. It is made from a standard iron ring plunged into a magic Tea solution.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6794,'en','If you''re looking for something to trample those flowers growing in your fields, these boots are just the ticket. Your feet mightn''t smell so bad with them on. It''s a shame they don''t come as shorts too.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6795,'en','If you''re planning to go to one of those eternally popular BABA theme-nights, this cloak is just what you need.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6796,'en','With this petal-peppered belt around your waist, you can slip out of a nasty situation while your enemies roll around the ground laughing. This will take care of the most war-weary Chafer army, and instantly reverse the situation to your advantage.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6797,'en','If you have always dreamt of being a florist and having rose-scented breath, it''s time for you to put this strange headgear on.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6799,'en','Sharp as a Bwork blade, the Bwork Chief''s blade has the advantage of being much heavier. It is certainly less easy to handle, but you just have to make it fall on your opponent and he''ll be in two pieces. Lifting it up again if you miss is another issue, but your enemy will surely have run off by then.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6800,'en','This cloak is made of Gobball Wool. It''s neither classy nor attractive. Don''t bother with it, basically.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6801,'en','A pretty, warm, powerfully smelling lining was sewn beautifully onto an ordinary cape. Around your shoulders, or lain in front of a roaring fire like a Gobball-skin rug, you''ll find some use for this cape.
Eventually.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6802,'en','These very soft earmuffs will keep your big flappy ears nice and warm.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6804,'en','Although basic looking, this flinty amulet is endowed with a very powerful magic that can turn a Bwork into a princess... or the opposite, nobody knows.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6805,'en','With this little thing on your wrist, even your good friends will think you''ve married a great Bwork Chief. It''s enough to get you a few free drinks at the local inn... Don''t be fooled though, they''ll be pity drinks.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6807,'en','These boots just look like ordinary Bwork boots. And yet, they are Chief Bwork''s boots. Hard-wearing, powerful, and smelly, they will be the deciding factor in any evenly-matched battle.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6811,'en','With this ragged cloak you''ll look like a battle-weary Bwork warrior. It''s perfect for stealing lunch-money off the elderly in the village. All the same, if you''re in search of a soul mate, you might want to change your approach... unless you wear it with nothing else on... Hey, that''s it... that way, you can keep on scaring the elderly of the village too! Kill two birds with the same stones.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6812,'en','These purple leather briefs are all you need, you can wear them on their own and still look distinguished, provided that they fit you. You''re better off keeping still in them, though - even the slightest movement will have you sounding like an old door creaking shut.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6813,'en','If you really want to look like a weakling, this helmet is made for you. In your case, it mightn''t make too much difference all the same.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6817,'en','This amazing amulet was made from a Reptilian Shield, from which all gems were removed. As a result, it''s a particularly heavy, but very sturdy, piece of jewellery. Your neck will be protected from vampire-bites, as well as from the aggressive advances of female villagers.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6819,'en','This bracelet looks strangely like a glove... it''s not a glove, it''s a bracelet.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6821,'en','Made from the remains of a Chief Crocodyl, this weapon will prove very useful if you are handsome, deft, clever and strong enough to handle it. In your case, I would try to find someone who will trade it for a Twiggy Sword.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6825,'en','These beautiful slippers, made of Chief Crocodyl''s skin and scales, come with sharp teeth at their ends. Be careful when you play footsie under the table with your beloved, you might tear off her lovely Tabi woollen stockings.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6830,'en','The first day back to school after the holidays is tough for any child, but for Iops, it''s as though they die a little inside every time it happens. This bag makes the whole experience that bit easier to bear.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6831,'en','Too stiff to be used as a whip, too flexible to cause any real bodily harm, this gem-covered belt nevertheless serves one obscure purpose... Armed with this, you''ll never find your pants around your ankles again. Great or what?');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6834,'en','If you''ve always dreamt of looking like a Crocodyl - without becoming one - then this headgear''s make for you. Don''t even think about using this headgear to fool your friends and tell them you''ve actually killed a Crocodyl. They''ll never believe you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6839,'en','This weapon, on which Meow Meow put his hallmark, could turn you into a legendary Ecaflip, eventually...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6840,'en','This weapon, on which Meow Meow put his hallmark, could turn you into a legendary Ecaflip... maybe...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6863,'en','The helmet of an Astrubian mercenary.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6886,'en','The cloak of an Astrubian mercenary... what were you expecting?');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6894,'en','This super-mighty fighting Bow Meow is the embodiment of super-might. Very impressive. Beware, it can only be entrusted to the care of Game Masters... because they''re worth it.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6895,'en','Less super-mighty than the super-mighty fighting Bow Meow, this small fighting Bow Meow is still very powerful. This pet remains a safe bet for Game Masters but it''s not the least bit house trained and tends to roll around in its own detritus. Don''t forget to throw some boiling water over it every once in a while so that it retains its splendour.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6908,'en','Hairy but elegant, this belt should remind you of your lady-love.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6909,'en','These are the perfect boots for splashing around in the mud or making big dents in an expensive hardwood floor. It''s forbidden to wear them on dance floors, beaches and in saunas.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6910,'en','This ring used to be fixed on the legs of rutting boars so that breeders could easily recognize them. Today, you are the one wearing the ring. You can take from with what you wish...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6911,'en','This ridiculously small ring will help you overcome your Arachnophobia once and for all.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6912,'en','Made from the rotting remains of decaying Arachnees, you''ll just love this belt. From time to time, it might come back to life and greedily bite you on the hips. Bloody thing!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6913,'en','With this Arachelmet on, you will look like a wild Arachnee. What will that achieve? Well, you might scare off some flies...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6914,'en','Did you know that Weak Arachnees only have four hairy legs? With only four blows of this axe, you could turn one into an Arachneetrunk. Blimey. Imagine everyone in Amakna doing that. It explains why you don''t see Weak Arachnees any more, anyway.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6915,'en','This is such a light ring that your hands can perform acrobatic feats when it''s on. It''s also quite useful if you want to humiliate somebody smaller than you by smashing their head with your thumb.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6916,'en','Made out of Moskito skin and wings, this bag used to be a big fad in schools. Today, it is old-fashioned and has been replaced by the Small Chief Crocodyl schoolbag. I don''t get it - one, a Small Chief Crocodyl bag is much more expensive and two, it''s HORRIBLE. Kids these days.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6917,'en','This headgear takes its name from the eccentric Enutrof who discovered it while stripping a sick old Moskito for all it had. Extremely useful for inexperienced adventurers, this headgear will help you seduce famished Arachnees.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6918,'en','This small amulet is not as effective as the famous Arachnamu. It certainly looks good, though... To be worn on a bare, hairy chest for a great jewel-in-the-roughage look.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6919,'en','The Mush Mush has a reputation for being a nasty piece of work. He''ll pester and bite you at every opportunity, and he''s very moody. I was married to someone like that once... Smelled like mushrooms too...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6920,'en','When a Mush Mush gets married, he gives this wedding ring to his bride. Since the bride has no arms, the ring is put delicately on one of its thorns. If you get hold of this ring, you will forever break the sacred bond between the two creatures. At best, the Mush Mush will take you as his bride to make up for it, and just remember, Mush Mushes spend their whole lives where the sun don''t shine...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6921,'en','Before the prohibition, Musheadgear was smoked or drunk as tea. This headgear really has it all.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6922,'en','The only thing more impressive than a livid Mush Mush is a livid Mush Mush in a cloak. Indeed, this particular cloak is the embodiment of a certain kind of ultra-powerful clothing... pretty ugly clothing if you ask me.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6923,'en','This amulet used to belong to the great robber "Thisme" who was famous for his limitless cruelty and idiotic death. A central figure of Eniripsa folklore, he was crushed and drowned to death in an olive press having just come out of jail after a 30-year sentence for the theft of a giant walnut.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6924,'en','These sharp daggers are very popular among robbers and very unpopular among the elderly for one and the same reason. The daggers cast spells that let them steal Kamas from adversaries. At least that''s the story their victims tell.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6925,'en','This beautiful belt is essential you if you ever decide to become a highwayman. Don''t wear it round town, though, you''ll be arrested on sight.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6926,'en','With this prespwig on, you''ll look like Debbie Crockett, the most celebrated huntress of the modern age, but a tragic victim of premature baldness. That''s not to say that this rat-bitten, off-red wig is any better than a balding nut.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6927,'en','This reddish small cloak can be also used as a rug or doormat so that you can redecorate the house on the cheap.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6928,'en','This ring, both simple and original, will seduce adventurers who long for the good things in life but could never afford them. The kind who would beat the daylights out of helpless animals and strip them of anything resembling an ornament. There''s no shortage of them, believe me.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6929,'en','The Prespic Belt is the ideal belt for keeping your hips warm. It itches like hell, though... you wanna be hard to wear this one!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6930,'en','This helmet directly hewed in stone is worth its weight in gold. It will both protect you from the attacks of a Crackrock and allow you to give head butts worthy of that of Desirock. It''s perfect to make your opponents go off their rocker.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6931,'en','This stone cloak is a bit too stiff, but you''ll be grateful when you''re in danger of being spat on by a Crackler.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6933,'en','Incredibly heavy but equally effective, these rocky boots will give you a good excuse to drag your feet when you have to defend a Perceptor in a fight you know you can''t win.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6934,'en','This amulet is as heavy as a bulimic Blop. It has not been designed for weak adventurers. However, once you get used to bearing its heavy weight around your neck, you''ll sure cut a dash!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6935,'en','Wear it on your waist and you''ll gain the respect of your peers. Wear it on your head and you''ll be the laughing stock of Astrub');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6936,'en','With this helmet on, you''ll be able to pretend to be a Scaraleaf hunter.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6937,'en','With this helmet on, your friends will think that you''ve joined the elite Scaraleaf hunter clan.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6938,'en','With this helmet on, your friends will think that you''ve joined the elite Scaraleaf hunter clan.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6939,'en','With this helmet on, your friends will think that you''ve joined the elite Scaraleaf hunter clan.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6940,'en','Have you ever dreamt of wearing a cape made of Scaraleaf shells? Well, here''s your chance! Once equipped, you should feel as if you were a real Scaraleaf and you might even succeed to slide and skid around. This should be enough to take aback a whole herd of Trools.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6941,'en','Who''s never dreamt of wearing a cloak made of Scareleaf shells? Once equipped, you''ll probably believe yourself to be a true Scaraleaf, and maybe you''ll manage to move on by way of slipping and skidding. That''s enough to take a crowd of Trools aback.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6942,'en','Who''s never dreamt of wearing a cloak made of Scareleaf shells? Once equipped, you''ll probably believe yourself to be a true Scaraleaf, and maybe you''ll manage to move along by way of slipping and skidding. That''s enough to take a crowd of Trools aback.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6943,'en','Who''s never dreamt of wearing a cloak made of Scareleaf shells? Once equipped, you''ll probably believe yourself to be a true Scaraleaf, and maybe you''ll manage to move along by way of slipping and skidding. That''s enough to take a crowd of Trools aback.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6944,'en','When you''ll wear this ring, you''ll spare a thought for all the Scaraleaves you have wiped out. You then maybe ask yourself if it is worth this slaughter... Yeah, of course it is worth it!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6945,'en','When you''ll wear this ring, you''ll spare a thought for all the Scaraleaves you have wiped out. You then maybe ask yourself if it is worth this slaughter... Yeah, of course it is worth it!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6946,'en','When you''ll wear this ring, you''ll spare a thought for all the Scaraleaves you have wiped out. You then maybe ask yourself if it is worth this slaughter... Yeah, of course it is worth it!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6947,'en','When you''ll wear this ring, you''ll spare a thought for all the Scaraleaves you have wiped out. You then maybe ask yourself if it is worth this slaughter... Yeah, of course it is worth it!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6948,'en','The Scarabelt was worn as an indicator of a warrior''s fist-fighting skills. With a Green Scarabelt, your enemy knew you were a beginner. A red one meant that you were a lusty warrior who ate the uncooked internal organs of your enemies just for fun... And the white one indicated that you were really tough. A blue one meant you didn''t spend long enough saving up for one of the others.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6949,'en','The Scarabelt was worn as an indicator of a warrior''s fist-fighting skills. With a Green Scarabelt, your enemy knew you were a beginner. A red one meant that you were a lusty warrior who ate the uncooked internal organs of your enemies just for fun... And the white one indicated that you were really tough. A blue one meant you didn''t spend long enough saving up for one of the others.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6950,'en','The Scarabelt was worn as an indicator of a warrior''s fist-fighting skills. With a Green Scarabelt, your enemy knew you were a beginner. A red one meant that you were a lusty warrior who ate the uncooked internal organs of your enemies just for fun... And the white one indicated that you were really tough. A blue one meant you didn''t spend long enough saving up for one of the others.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6951,'en','The Scarabelt was worn as an indicator of a warrior''s fist-fighting skills. With a Green Scarabelt, your enemy knew you were a beginner. A red one meant that you were a lusty warrior who ate the uncooked internal organs of your enemies just for fun... And the white one indicated that you were really tough. A blue one meant you didn''t spend long enough saving up for one of the others.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6952,'en','With this Boowolf hat on your head, you''ll have a good excuse for your stinky breath!!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6953,'en','These boots are coated with Boowolf hair. They are extremely useful for cleaning dusty wooden floors or fixing up the heads of your enemies as they lie dead on the battle field.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6954,'en','This Boowolf fur makes for excellent protection against the cold... and also adventurers with a highly developed sense of smell.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6955,'en','Used as a whip, this thong can be a lot more efficient than it looks to motivate your fellow travellers when they''ve lost the will to live.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6956,'en','Beware! This ring will make your finger stink. Although this foul smell may cover a worse smell... This may be the best thing that could happen to your finger... and your hands in general in fact.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6957,'en','This sword used to cut the granite blocks for the city walls of Bonta and Brakmar. Nowadays, it''s used to crush creatures in battle.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6958,'en','Eternally fashionable, this hat will give you a unique look - a long, discreet look up the skirts of the Cra women. Perfect for those warm summer night parties.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6961,'en','This ring is as popular with dentists as it is with gangsters. They both use it to break the teeth of careless people... They both use similar drills too, but let''s not dwell on that...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6971,'en','This hat is quite a good replica of the famous Clint. It will perfectly suit mercenary disciples who are convinced they are master material.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6975,'en','This ultra-powerful hat is the Mercenary emblem. It has the power to protect you from both the rain and the sun... a good start at least.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6978,'en','From a distance, this creature looks just like a Bow Wow. A simple glance at its head and you can see it''s been through terrible trials... which eventually led it to become a vegetarian and to subscribe for life to the Pet Sanctuary Foundation. As such, it will only eat vegetables and plants that grow on Pandala island.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000059,'en','From a distance, this creature looks just like a Bow Wow. A simple glance at its head and you can see it''s been through terrible trials... which eventually led it to become a vegetarian and to subscribe for life to the Pet Sanctuary Foundation. As such, it will only eat vegetables and plants that grow on Pandala island.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6980,'en','This Dofus was laid by a dragon which decided to remain anonymous. Even the wisest adventurers still wonder why.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6981,'en','The blade of these daggers is made of ice. Reminds me of an old incident that had the detectives working overtime... A fella called Tum Sellick stabbed his buddy with one of these things over a couple of Kamas... Nice crime... They found the novelty ice-cube maker in his house though... NICKED!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6982,'en','These daggers are soaked in the blood of various evil creatures, such as children. They are very special.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6983,'en','Only sharpened once every ten years, these daggers retain their lethal edge because of the dark magic that possesses them. They can sometimes be seen walking the streets at the weekend, playing loud music and staring threateningly at passersby.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6984,'en','These daggers belonged to a Sadida whose dazzling ascent will be remembered forever in Amaknan history. From a young age, this Sadida dedicated his humble life to Gobbly hunting... the villagers found it hilarious... word spread and soon folk came from all around to watch him hunt those ridiculous balls of wool. His revenge was terrible and long-lived. When the price of Gobbly skins skyrocketed, he became so rich that he paid to have every last villager who mocked him hunted down and murdered. He''s storing their skins too, but the stock market isn''t going his way.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6986,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6988,'en','The sister of a wild Xelor who was kidnapped by unscrupulous slave drivers used to wear this thing for her nightly shows, the nature of which I will not repeat here.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6989,'en','This hat was made a long time ago by apprentice tailors who wanted to protect themselves from the violent fits of rage of Mirko, their boss. This fine business man was often forced to kick his apprentices in the head when they didn''t work fast enough. From what I''ve heard, that was far too good for the lazy bast...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6990,'en','This hat is a tribute to the distant cousins of the Moskitoes: the Moths. A lot bigger and a lot kinder than the Moskitoes, the Moths took such good care of their livestock that they soon became extinct from self-inflicted famine. From this tragic story, we have the common insult ''Moth'' as in, ''Poor bloody Moth'', which describes a fellow who discovers his spouse is devastatingly gluttonous...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6991,'en','This strange-looking hat looks like a big dehydrated rotting fruit... A bit like you after a night out at the pub.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6992,'en','An improved version of the famous Kanniball mask, the Kannipiwi will make you look like a real Piwi hunter to your friends.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6993,'en','Lonard Kohen, the famous minstrel with the voice of a castrated Crackler (which is still incredibly low) was burnt alive in front of the bank of Bonta after causing a moral scandal with his latest, and last, song "Tower of Thong". A full recording was made of his cries of agony, which he had the vision to frame in C#m, modulate to Fb, and resolve in a risqué but manageable G#. Niiice.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6994,'en','This hood-cloak hybrid is just amazing. If it was made of leather, Captain Chafer would have loved it.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6995,'en','You just can''t stay inside this cape, it''ll throw you out whether you want to go or not.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6996,'en','Stradamus was an old drunken Enutrof who could read the future in pints of beer. Legend has it he was buried standing up in a wall of the Brakmar inn upon his own request, "so that no drunkard can ever spill his beer over my grave". This has been told at least once a week by every drunk in every inn in Brakmar. That''s a lot. God I hate that story.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6997,'en','The woman who created this ring was convinced the end of the world was near due to plummeting food supplies. She used to spend entire days engraving messages on wooden tables with her motto ''No steak but what we bake''. Time proved her wrong.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6998,'en','This small wedding ring will fit an Eniripsa''s little fingers perfectly. For Iops, however, it''s almost unusable. Their fingers are too fat and they can''t get it into their heads that it''s not a bracelet.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(6999,'en','Lahilama was a great spiritual guide who kept his temple right in the heart of the mountains. He was so bored that he spent his days sewing little yellow hats for his disciples. They just had nothing to talk about. They all slowly went mad years of awkward conversation.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7000,'en','This ridiculous little piece of bamboo has the strangest magical powers. It used to be worn by young Pandawas, once their puberty came to an end. You might want to wait another couple of years yourself before you slip it around your neck...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7001,'en','"I, I am the kheeng, you, you are the quheen, whee can be heeroes just for one daaaayyyy..." 
Davyd, famous minstrel, was singing his head off on his way back from Moon Island...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7002,'en','This amulet of Bamboo resin will spread a nice smell all around you. It comes in handy when you''re practising your Wind of Panic.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7003,'en','This Talisman was created with stardust and precious stones, encased in Ancestral Treechnid Amber. The mixture can be quite explosive, so it is not recommended you try to make it yourself. Leave it to a Jeweller you don''t like.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7011,'en','This cloak is made of red beard hair... it is quite unique. Animated by extraordinarily powerful magic that renders it all but living, it adores playing practical jokes on the unfortunate bugger who puts it on. It''s favourite trick? It unfindably conceals itself when it senses you need it most. If you do ever manage to discipline it, it can be very powerful in fights. As the Wabbits like to say it''s a "weal good instwument of wawfawe".');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7012,'en','This Amulet is, in fact, a candy. It might have been edible if it hadn''t been carefully rolled under female Bworker armpits for 36 generations as part of some bizarre ritual.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7022,'en','This Staff belonged to Sangroku''s grandfather, Sangrokrane, famous for his big head. Legend says this magic staff has the ability to stretch to any length desired... use it to flatten your enemies or stick it down your pants, you''re always a winner with this thing...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7029,'en','Sangroku ate way too many magic beans one time. Forever more, it was a constant struggle to restrain the winds of panic that erupted from his britches without the slightest warning... Those very same winds made him famous the length and breadth of Amakna.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7031,'en','Poor Flooey lost his mind after a terrible fight against Many. Fortunately, his amulet didn''t suffer. It kept both its mesmerizing properties and its laxative powers. To be taken only when absolutely necessary.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7034,'en','Passed down from generation to generation, this misshapen helmet was even worn by Crail himself. Many adventurers think it has mysterious powers. As with many divinities and modern heroes, the magical powers of this helmet have all the potency of a shoe...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7037,'en','This stick used to belong to Granny Candy, one of the three famous Love Priestesses. Sharpened at one end and shiny at the other, this stick is renowned for its versatility and its annoying tendency to turn up just about anywhere. None can resist its power.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7038,'en','This crown belonged to the famous King Jellix, renowned for his unbounded romanticism and his seductive power which left its mark on many female Jellies... Some even say he is the father of all the Jellies of the region of Amakna, proof (if needed) of his stamina and legendary fecundity.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7039,'en','A famous Sunday fighter, Frank crossed over into martial arts after he failed miserably at his stone-cutter apprenticeship.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7040,'en','This bow belonged to Kuri, the famous Love Priestess and left-hand woman of Granny Candy. Never turn your back on a Love Priestess. One arrow from this bow is enough to tear your heart to shreds, or your arse if you have actually turned around.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7043,'en','Legend says that this magnificent Dofus came out of the frozen hole of the Water dragon Aguabrial. Legend does not say if he had a cold that day, though it''s highly likely.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7056,'en','This unique hat used to belong to a Xelor grandmaster, known the world over for his explosive theories and his incessant meddling with time. His death was as explosive and untimely as his life... Jealous of his neighbour''s hat, whose magic powers were said to be even greater than his, he rashly unleashed a Wind of Panic to remove it forever, forgetting about his own. He was blown into a million little pieces when his hat exploded like a giant firecracker.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7058,'en','This headgear is made of dead dried Kralove leftovers. Be careful, it can come back to life if you use it as a bathing cap.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7069,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7070,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7071,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7072,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7073,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7074,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7075,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7076,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7077,'en','This porous but absorbent yellow shield was made from the remains of a creature who used to live in a Pineapple Mask at the bottom of the sea.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7078,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7079,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7080,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7081,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7082,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7083,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7084,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7085,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7086,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7087,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7088,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7089,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7090,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7091,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7092,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7093,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7094,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7097,'en','This Shield is given to disciples who don''t know how to correctly use a Shield yet.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7098,'en','This hammer is indispensible to blacksmiths.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7102,'en','The Ice Knight was famous for being one of the greatest sword smiths in all of Amakna. Only Liche the unmerciful refused to recognize his talent. Offended by this creature''s ignorance, the Ice Knight stopped working, refusing to forge so much as a teaspoon until she agreed to publicly recognize his talent. The Ice Knight worked the bars around Amakna for a couple of hundred years, but the local economy never crumbled as he had expected, nor did Amakna''s military influence waver... as he had also expected. When he finally took up his rusty hammer once more, he found he''d completely forgotten his former skill. This ridiculous sword was his last usable creation.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7103,'en','This Wand was used to behead all the ninnies in Amakna. Suffice it to say it''s seen a lot of action. It''s interesting to note how much it resembles a staff or even a walking stick... It might have even been used to satisfy the wicked fantasies of the owner who named it. No one will ever have the last final word on this sordid story.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7104,'en','These flee-flops were used to practice various martial arts. Not quite revolutionary and artistically speaking, a failure, they were only good for running away, a bit like yourself...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7106,'en','With this Larva head round your neck, you look like Stive Irween, the famous modern-day larva tamer.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7107,'en','You probably never dreamt of putting your feet right inside the guts of a Larva... But here is your chance... Seize it!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7108,'en','This plain bag used to be very fashionable a very long time ago. It is the best example of your ancestors'' bad taste.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7109,'en','You finally have the chance to look like a real larva. You will be able to openly show the world your larvian lifestyle.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7110,'en','This terrific Wand is made of larva guts which are firstly dried, then enchanted and finally rehydrated. It''s totally shapeless. A bit like you, except you''re not even enchanted.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7112,'en','The only way to get an egg like this is to force a black dragon to mate with a white dragon. Although some people paint ordinary eggs this colour at home... You may have been tricked.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7113,'en','This Dofus is worryingly similar to a wild Dragoturkey egg... For once, appearances might not be misleading.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7114,'en','As dark as darkness can be, as solid as a rock, the Dragon which laid such an egg probably didn''t forget too quickly.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7115,'en','The Ivory Dofus is incomparably white, which isn''t surprising given that Dardondakal the White Dragon whitened it with his breath every morning (an old trick passed on to him from his Dragon grandmother).');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7116,'en','The enchantment in this ring is very strange - once around your finger, the only person you''ll be able to talk to will be the jeweller who made it.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7117,'en','A particularly talentless group of cosmopolitan minstrels used this type of ring to keep time at their shows after their original drummer left them. They would all put a ring on a toe, and beat in time. Needless to say, it was the percussion that always let them down.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7118,'en','This big moth-shaped ring won''t make your hands pretty, but isn''t that a good thing?');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7119,'en','The jeweller who created this masterpiece is no relative of the famous Sword Smith, despite appearances. No one ever understood what the designer said about using the ring...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7120,'en','Contrary to common misunderstanding, this ring has nothing to do with the beautiful Karin, whose regular live shows at Sufokia Pirates'' Inn raised many a visiting spirit from the dead. The namesake of this jewel is a musician who breeds Tofus in his spare time... so what, you ask. Well, with this ring, it''ll sound like there''s a dying tofu attached to your finger.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7121,'en','This living ring has a terrible curse that makes even the toughest of adventurers seriously ill. They say it was originally designed to heal the person who wore it, but since warriors brought it to the most disreputable locations in the land, its sense of dignity led it to become more and more dangerous and aggressive.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7122,'en','This ring is made for tearful novices. It also symbolizes some ancient, unspeakable traditions. It''s made for you! Perfect.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7123,'en','For experienced adventurers only. It might shock your family and friends to know it''s composed of young, innocent creatures.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7128,'en','Spiteful gossips claim that this ring is the most useful fashion accessory in the world. The wings attached to it can be quite a pain when you need to get a tissue out of your pocket. Now, Iops neither have tissues nor pockets... so, it''s just fine.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7131,'en','Many other adventurers dreamt of getting their paws on this jewel long before you came along. Indeed, it''s said to have many powers, such as the power to turn fierce warriors into good-for-nothing dreamers. It says in my book to never put it near fire. Doesn''t say why...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7132,'en','This ring owes its name to the last words pronounced by its creator: "O'' Ring Ami! You''re such a friend!" he said in a painful but bewitching rattle. It is interesting to note that this Bamboo ring was actually made before Bamboo evolved. Another mystery which will not be solved for another ten years or so!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7136,'en','This medal used to belong to a famous Pandawa master at an old martial arts school who taught his disciples the principles of defence using their opponents'' strength. His school finally closed down because his opponents were no longer strong enough.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7137,'en','This Cape was hand-sewn for one single reason: to stop you from sleeping for weeks on end. It is so rigid that it will keep you standing still and upright no matter what happens. Just don''t try to tie your shoelaces.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7138,'en','Worn by the most important people in the world, this cloak is famous for its legendary softness which means you don''t have to put on underwear in the warm season. An elegant way to expose yourself...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7139,'en','The shoemaker loved strolling in the fields, looking for improbable love. Instead of finding her soul mate, she died falling into a huge ditch full of filth, close to the Pig Zone. Her body was found seventy years later, when they finally emptied the ditch. Her brother apparently said: "We all have to go sometime", before falling into the ditch himself.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7140,'en','Contrary to appearances, Xena was not a warrior, but a shoemaker. Her generous figure and her unlimited passion for housework strongly suggested a brilliant career in the inns of Amakna. But it wasn''t to be.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7141,'en','This strange hat will protect you from sun beams, especially when its dark. Be careful though, every thirty years it comes to life and tries to suffocate its owner... It doesn''t say when the last time... I wouldn''t worry about it...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7142,'en','This hat was used by some Xelors to hide their hereditary baldness. Enutrofs used it to hide their wives'' faces. In fact, the only male syndrome it doesn''t treat is prostate cancer...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7143,'en','The Solomonk hat was worn by the Chief of a Pandawa tribe. Experts in laxative potions, low-ranking Pandawas were often obliged to test the potions for the alchemists. When banished to the jungle for these trials, this hat doubled as a chamber pot, reducing their load considerably.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7144,'en','This wedding hat has gone out of fashion, its lace is no longer considered stylish. If it was recycled into knickers and worn on a hairy head, it might still get a reaction out of a Chafer.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7145,'en','Gaddie, a strange creature from an imaginary world, always stood out for its incredible cunning, its total aversion to plants and its ability to fast for days on end in times of war. A creature that complex to understand was obviously impossible to control. It was abandoned in the depths of the Mines of Kruup where its only friend was an old, Gobbly devouring Liche.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7146,'en','This headgear looks like any old wig, but it is powerful indeed. It has one prior owner who had the strange and despicable habit of dressing up as other people, and conning the elderly into signing over items of tiny value. Once he convinced a gentle old man that he was his dead wife returned to life, proceeded to ''remarry'' him, had six of his children (which even I can''t explain) and then, ten years later, just as they were about to renew their vows on a scenic cliffside, he broke the news. It is said he ran off with three party poppers and a half-eaten ball of Stracciatella ice-cream, laughing wildly... still laughing as he tripped and fell over the cliff and laughing to this day if you believe the popular but unlikely sea shanty, ''The crazy fool took my Stracciatella''.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7150,'en','This hat, strangely named, belonged to a poor Ecaflip who became mute after a traumatic event. An artist through and through, he was compelled to follow a Brewer training. When he turned 14, he drowned in a barrel of beer and tears. Fortunately, beer was not wasted as the priest who was in charge of the funeral fell into an alcoholic coma for many years before he could take his office right where he had stopped it.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7151,'en','On the box of this helmet, it said: ''This giant clay protective headgear will turn you into a giant with a head of clay''. Upon further study, you''ll realize the helmet is not made of clay, but of lead. Every year, many adventurers die, trapped under the helmet like nipples under a Chinese fire cup...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7152,'en','This basin-shaped hat was used by the firemen of Amakna when there were fires on cereal fields. Nowadays it is mainly used by brewers and pub waitresses who are treated like walking barrels.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7153,'en','This huge hammer makes a very loud noise when hitting a Iop''s skull as it tends to amplify sound. As surprising as it is effective.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7154,'en','This light hammer is designed for small beings. Xelors used to find great pleasure in squashing Arachnees with this implement. Its use quickly changed and it became a little toy for young Iop Handymen.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7155,'en','For fifty long years, the famous Captain Adock used this terrible Hammer to slay anyone who got in his way - including women and children. In spite of his legendary bad temper and his addiction to alcohol, he won the respect of all warriors - both friend and enemy.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7156,'en','This rusty hammer is perfect for all your smashing needs - pulverize maple trees, atomize Moskitoes, this hammer does it all.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7157,'en','This hammer was used to sound the bell of the Church of Amakna every Sunday. In these times of war, it''s used much more often than that.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7158,'en','This hammer was crafted by a famous alchemist during his sentence in the prison of Brakmar. He planned to steal his competitors'' secrets and get rich when he got out. This hammer was the first in a collection of devilish instruments.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7159,'en','As the Enutrof philosopher Traincartes once said, "I think, therefore I hammer." It sums up the way this greedy bunch sees the world.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7160,'en','Many ages ago, this Bow was occupied with a very dark magic, a mysterious force that strikes fear into both its owners and its targets in equal measure.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7161,'en','This bow was mainly used to hunt Plain Boars. Indeed, it is so powerful that it can kill several young boars with one single arrow, provided that they stand still in a line. Well it could happen!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7162,'en','This Bow belonged to an independent group of Minstrels mainly famous for their war cries which destroyed their enemies'' ear drums. They were firstly banished to Pandala, but after driving generations of Pandawa nuts, they were finally brought to the Great Sorlok to be slowly digested for more than 752 years.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7163,'en','This bow was used as a dissuasive weapon. The owner of the Runaway Bow claimed that he was using poisoned arrows so any cowards he met would take off instantly.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7164,'en','Light and fragile, this bow appeals to adventurers who are more concerned about appearances than substance.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7165,'en','This explosive wand was dipped into the lava of an erupting volcano before being sculpted, and then enchanted. It goes without saying that it''s very powerful... despite its ridiculous appearance.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7167,'en','The craftsman who created this wand had many apprentices. He made them work all day long. He was supposed to teach them the tricks of the trade but as it turned out, he was a terrible teacher. He always started sentences, trailed off, fell asleep, dreamt he was a goat and started licking the blackboard. I''m not suggesting that there''s a link between the last two... I''m just reading the... psychiatric... report. OH MAN, this guy was messed up in the head... Blimey!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7168,'en','Once sculpted, this wand was soaked in beer for many decades ''to put a few magical powers into it'', as the people who made it said. Unfortunately, it started to rot, but it has a few magical properties... it can lure worms to the earth''s surface for example. Are you into fishing by any chance?');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7169,'en','Ideal for lighting a fire, or indeed lighting up a dreary party. With this wand, you just might get the chance to shine once in your life. An opportunity not to be missed.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7170,'en','Creizy the pastry chef was nuts... he married Stufh the Lumberjane and choked her to death the very next day with his fat-stuffed pastries. Ever since, the phrase "Creizy Stufh" is used to express an unhappy surprise after a great celebration.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7171,'en','The designer of this wand kept forgetting to pick his kids up at school. Conscious of his absent-mindedness, he sculpted a wand that would come to life everyday and remind him to pick his kids up. After a while, he kept thinking the wand was waking him up to remind him to go to the bathroom. His children were taken away from him not long after.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7172,'en','This magic wand is still used today to empty septic tanks, clean out ditches and pick noses. Most informed sculptors will tell you that it derives all its magic from all the filthy waste it''s been dragged through... in reality, it''s the dirty gunge from your snout.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7173,'en','This terrific Wand can wrap itself round your opponent''s neck and strangle them slowly but surely. An original and distinguished way of killing enemies you don''t respect.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7174,'en','This cloak is essential if you want to practice Pandawushu...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7176,'en','Maxx Evanz, master staff carver, is the fellow who created this little wonder. It can darken the sky with raging cloud and draw the blood of your enemies... even if they don''t have any. Legend says it took him nine years to carve. Even your enemies will have to complement you on this beautiful piece of stuff.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7177,'en','With this Pandawushu Headband around your skull, you''ll be able to scare away young Lenalds pretending to be martial arts Masters. Don''t forget to bawl a bit of a war cry to be more convincing.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7178,'en','If it wasn''t for the incessant arguing over whether this thing is a fruit or a root, it would be an excellent weapon.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7181,'en','Red was a young Sadidette. She loved singing, though she had a terrible voice. She always dreamt of travelling to Chili. She was often sent packing but never got anywhere...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7182,'en','Mel was quite unlucky. Her husband was a lazy cad, incapable of assuming his status as the head of the family. She was convinced that incessant nagging was the way to go... "You''ll get no strawberry jelly if you don''t go harvest that barley" or "You''ll get no tobacco till you''ve sheared those Gobballs" and so on. Obviously, this story has nothing to do with this very powerful root... unless it starts to nag you too...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7183,'en','This Root has a purity that is the essence of perfection for some wide-eyed craftsmen. I can tell you from experience that this root is the single greatest cause of marital breakdown in the entire region.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7184,'en','This terrible root is mainly known for its capacity to provoke climatic disasters at the exact place where it''s been used. Avoid using it to kick your enemies around... It is an abuse which could see you and all your friends burnt to a crisp, drowned in a flood, blown to bits, frozen solid, misted to... well the last one wouldn''t be so bad, but just don''t use it okay!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7185,'en','Using this root during a fight is supposed to be very easy. Nevertheless, it can happen that the root somehow comes to life and does whatever it wants... that''s generally when the owner yells "This is not the usual Root ''Een, is it?". Well, it is indeed the usual Root ''Een.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7187,'en','This bow is reviled the land over for leading its archers into battle at the slightest sign of unusual behaviour. Drinking loudly, shaking hands for longer than is proper, and wearing hats - a few examples of what can make the bow start shooting wildly.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7188,'en','These Daggers are often used to cut the ground right out from under your enemies'' feet. An original way to surprise them which often comes to a messy end.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7189,'en','This strange staff is an improved version of the famous God Rod. Indeed, this staff was designed and made according to the numerous tests done on the God Rod by the Love Priestesses. This model was even used by Kuri herself, which makes it a unique piece.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7190,'en','When a precocious Sramette princess couldn''t find a single dagger that suited her, she offered a challenge to the dagger smiths of Amakna: the one who forged her a set capable of killing a Tofu in one blow would spend three nights in her bed... Unfortunately, not a single smith took up her challenge. By the time she found a willing craftsman, a retiree of the trade who never should have started in the first place, she''d been advertising her offer among other things on the streets of Madrestam for 17 years... Let''s just say that time hadn''t been kind to the proud Sramette.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7191,'en','Ramougre was an old Sram who became a jewellery master. He used this setter to perfect his creations as well as to murder his clients when he got bored. He was known for his bad temper, sometimes destroying his setter and his most beautiful creations. Today, when people with these daggers get angry, they pay tribute to Ramougre by cutting off some family jewels.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7192,'en','Grizmine never succeeded in properly using this Claw - she was always too drunk.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7193,'en','No one but Dark Vlad himself can use this sword properly, but if you carry it round town at least people will know you''re not one of those pathetic fools who died under its blade.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7194,'en','This bow proves that collaboration between technology and magic can lead to excellent results. This bow was quickly forgotten for some strange reason and its creator, Arkanum, had to close down his store.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7195,'en','This legendary sword was forged early one morning by a drunken Enutrof army, deep in the mines of Grimoth. It has a very powerful aura as well as a potent hum of beer.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7197,'en','This hammer was used to break chocolate blocks into dust for so many years, it eventually gained a delicious flavour. One more reason to give your enemies a taste!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7198,'en','Any old Enutrof will tell you that a well-maintained beard is every woman''s dream. This razor is so sharp it''ll even take care of that thick, curly back hair.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7199,'en','This sword belonged to a butcher called Franky Abatz who used it to disembowel his enemies for sausage meat. I used to go to that stall... Believe me, I made sure the dirty mongrel paid for every sausage he ever sold...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7200,'en','This magnificent sabre is used by Pandawushuka disciples when they reach the Shodanwa level alive.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7201,'en','This magnificent Sabre is used by Pandawushuka disciples when they reach the Nidanwa level alive.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7202,'en','This magnificent sabre is used by Pandawushuka disciples when they reach the Sandanwa level alive.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7203,'en','This magnificent sabre is used by Pandawushuka disciples when they reach the Yondanwa level alive.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7204,'en','This Staff is normally used by Pandawushuka disciples when they reach Shodanwa level without losing the use of their arms in the process.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7205,'en','This Staff is normally used by Pandawushuka disciples when they reach Nidanwa level without losing the use of their arms in the process.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7206,'en','This Staff is normally used by Pandawushuka disciples when they reach Sandanwa level without losing the use of their arms in the process.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7207,'en','This Staff is normally used by Pandawushuka disciples when they reach Yondanwa level without losing the use of their arms in the process.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7208,'en','This Axe is used by Pandawushuka disciples when they reach the Nidanwa level. It makes short work of Bamboo Forests, including anything that may be hiding in the undergrowth.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7209,'en','This Axe is used by Pandawushuka disciples when they reach the Nidanwa level. It makes short work of Bamboo Forests, including anything that may be hiding in the undergrowth.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7210,'en','This Axe is used by Pandawushuka disciples when they reach the Nidanwa level. It makes short work of Bamboo Forests, including anything that may be hiding in the undergrowth.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7211,'en','This axe is used by Pandawushuka disciples when they reach the Yondawa level. It makes short work of Bamboo forests, including anything that may be hiding in the undergrowth.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7212,'en','Equipped with this light and elegant Axe you''ll be able to progress more easily through the Bamboo Forests of Pandala. It will serve as sufficient protection against the warlike Pandis who never get tired of attacking lone Lumberjacks who wander through their lands.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7213,'en','This Shovel is supposed to cut through the soil at an incredible speed. Those who know how to handle it usually split their enemies'' skulls open instead.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7214,'en','These Sandals belonged to the Macians, an Ouginak tribe, which became extinct. They were so close to the Pandawas that, as the generations passed by, their fur slowly changed colour. One day, they were all killed by a horrible woman who wanted to make a coat out of them.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7215,'en','These thong sandals were formerly used by female Pandits to seduce lost adventurers and lure them into traps.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7216,'en','Those sandals are given to sick Pandawas for those special emergencies... we''re talking the dreaded McSheth, which usually comes a knocking when they drink too much down at the Inn.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7217,'en','Pandawas have always been attracted by alcoholic beverages. As time went by, they discovered how best to conserve and flavour them. These sandals were made especially for alcoholic Pandawas. They''re ballasted at the sole so that you can keep your feet firmly on the ground, most of the time. Good for fighting, terrible for running away...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7218,'en','Adin was a young Pandawa who loved collecting lamps, but he was far from being a genius.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7219,'en','Those sandals were awarded to young Pandits at the end of religious rituals. Nowadays they are mainly used for tap-dancing championships.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7221,'en','Tanukouï Sans wear this collar from early childhood. Given what these monsters are capable of, it''s no wonder this jewellery is so valuable.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7226,'en','From a distance, you''ll look like a Pandawushuka from the village of Akwadala with this hat on your head. Up close, you''ll look like an idiot.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7227,'en','From a distance, you''ll look like a Pandawushuka from the village of Terrdala with this hat on your head. Up close, you''ll look like an idiot.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7228,'en','From a distance, you''ll look like a Pandawushuka from the village of Feudala with this hat on your head. Up close, you''ll look like an idiot.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7229,'en','From a distance, you''ll look like a Pandawushuka from the village of Aerdala with this hat on your head. Up close, you''ll look like an idiot.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7230,'en','This cloak comes from Akwadala. It can be used as a doormat or even as a floorcloth if you''ve just come out of water.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7231,'en','This cloak comes from Terrdala Village. It can be used as a doormat or even as a towel if you''ve just come out of the water.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7232,'en','This cloak comes from Feudala. It can be used as a doormat or even as a towel if you''ve just come out of the water.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7233,'en','This cloak comes from Aerdala. It can be used as a doormat or even as a floorcloth if you''ve just come out of water.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7234,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7235,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7236,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7237,'en','This shield has seen a few battles too many, in this state it is good for nothing. Perhaps Bouwada, in Pandala village, could replace it for you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7238,'en','Pandawas from Akwadala always watch their figure. If you tighten this belt as much as possible, you should finally get some results with your flabby belly problem.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7239,'en','Pandawas from Terrdala always watch their figure. If you tighten this belt as much as possible, you should finally get some results with your flabby belly problem.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7240,'en','Pandawas from Feudala always watch their figure. If you tighten this belt as much as possible, you should finally get some results with your flabby belly problem.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7241,'en','Pandawas from Aerdala always watch their figure. If you tighten this belt as much as possible, you should finally get some results with your flabby belly problem.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7242,'en','These wooden Getas were made by the best shoemakers of the village of Akwadala. Since they''re quite open, your warts will be able to take a breath of fresh air and enjoy the landscape.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7243,'en','These wooden Getas were made by the best shoemakers in the village of Terrdala. Let your warts take a breath of fresh air and enjoy the landscape.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7244,'en','These wooden Geta were made by the best shoemakers in the village of Feudala. Since they''re quite open, your warts will be able to take a breath of fresh air and enjoy the landscape.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7245,'en','These wooden Getas were made by the best shoemakers in the village of Aerdala. Since they''re quite open, your warts will be able to take a breath of fresh air and enjoy the landscape.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7246,'en','This Wedding Ring comes from the village of Akwadala. More likely to be a lucky charm than a magic relic, you''ll still be able to make your friends believe you found your soul mate.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7247,'en','This Wedding Ring comes from the village of Terrdala. More likely to be a lucky charm than a magic relic, you''ll still be able to make your friends believe you''ve found your soul mate.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7248,'en','This Wedding Ring comes from the village of Feudala. More likely to be a lucky charm than a magic relic, you''ll still be able to make your friends believe you''ve found your soul mate.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7249,'en','This Wedding Ring comes from the village of Aerdala. More likely to be a lucky charm than a magic relic, you''ll still be able to make your friends believe you''ve found your soul mate.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7250,'en','The only people allowed to wear this amulet were the inhabitants of the village of Akwadala, as it was considered to be one of the most important parts of their traditional costume. Seen close up, you have to ask yourself why.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7251,'en','The only people allowed to wear this amulet were the inhabitants of the village of Terrdala, as it was considered to be one of the most important parts of their traditional costume. Seen close up, you have to ask yourself why.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7252,'en','The only people allowed to wear this amulet were the inhabitants of the village of Feudala, as it was considered to be one of the most important parts of their traditional costume. Seen close up, you have to ask yourself why.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7253,'en','The only people allowed to wear this amulet were the inhabitants of the village of Aerdala, as it was considered to be one of the most important parts of their traditional costume. Seen close up, you have to ask yourself why.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7254,'en','This staff was used to give young boisterous Pandawa a trashing. Three raps on the knuckles, fifteen lashes across the back, sixty blows to the head, two pokes in the eyes, that would be enough to calm them down a bit.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7255,'en','This axe, from the very beginning, was designed to cut living beings. Be careful! A single miscalculation and you could be cut in half!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7256,'en','As sharp as Moowolf claws, these daggers will turn you into a perfect apprentice assassin.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7257,'en','This Sabre was forged by Hotari Honza himself. It''s said to be one of his last creations before he took an intensive cooking course and became a chef. A collector''s item for sure!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7339,'en','This Kitsou cap can only be worn by adventurers who''ve lost their sense of smell. Don''t ask me why...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7340,'en','This wrap is river washable, even though it might fade after the third cycle.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7341,'en','This small Kitsou ring will protect you from casual troubles.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7342,'en','This Kitsou Amulet will draw attention to your double chin.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7368,'en','The designer of this wand kept forgetting to pick his kids up at school. Conscious of his absent-mindedness, he sculpted a wand that would come to life everyday and remind him to pick his kids up. After a while, he kept thinking the wand was waking him up to remind him to go to the bathroom. His children were taken away from him not long after.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7414,'en','This fluffy ball of hair scratches, bites, and pinches everything that comes close, including the hand that feeds it! It''s a terrifying yet irresistibly likeable and fascinating creature. Be careful, not only is this creature quick-tempered but it''s also quite picky about its diet. It only eats fresh meat from hunted creatures.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000050,'en','This fluffy ball of hair scratches, bites, and pinches everything that comes close, including the hand that feeds it! It''s a terrifying yet irresistibly likeable and fascinating creature. Be careful, not only is this creature quick-tempered but it''s also quite picky about its diet. It only eats fresh meat from hunted creatures.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7415,'en','This odd little creature only eats fresh fish. But don''t worry, its wholesome company more than makes up for the dehydrated-fish breath.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7422,'en','This exotic, fruit-shaped Mask is a real collector''s item. It has absolutely no use but you''ll look pretty original and tasty. People appreciate the effort.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7493,'en','This Setter will make the jewels you''ve created even more dazzling.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7495,'en','This magic Leather Cutter will enable you to cut leather and scrape skins better. It''s an ideal tool to improve old boots and belts.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7513,'en','Titude, a modest Enutrof Shoemaker, was even smaller than a Xelor. Legend says he created these sandals to be able to kiss his lady-love, a legless Eniripsa, on the lips.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7514,'en','Harry was an old wise man who spent his days fishing on the docks of Sufokia. His great moustache made him look like Danous Kwaide, famous actor of a theatre company that used to play at the Amakna Tavern. All this was only a prelude to incredible beer and meat ball orgies.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7515,'en','This cape doesn''t come from your Galaxy but it seems to match the colour of your Gobbly-wool fishnet stockings all the same.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7516,'en','It was an old unlucky bitter Enutrof who first discovered this terrible hat, hidden at the bottom of an alcove in the Bimd''Oule caves. Later, the Enutrof exiled himself far away from the Amakna lands to escape boredom and discover new horizons. Legend tells that he comes back to his native land once a century to make fun of his old friends... but we all know he''s a bit nostalgic.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7518,'en','This surprising creature comes from the afterlife and is not willing to go back there, unless it takes you with it...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000043,'en','This surprising creature comes from the afterlife and is not willing to go back there, unless it takes you with it...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7519,'en','This little dragon''s skin is as pink as a female Bwork''s backside, making it a risk-free and cheap way to fantasize in a private corner or to remind yourself of all those happy memories. This dragon isn''t just the object of your fantasies though, it''s also a very powerful and wise creature. However, you must be careful, as its hunger for other pets is as great as a Chafer''s perversion during a full moon.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000060,'en','This little dragon''s skin is as pink as a female Bwork''s backside, making it a risk-free and cheap way to fantasize in a private corner or to remind yourself of all those happy memories. This dragon isn''t just the object of your fantasies though, it''s also a very powerful and wise creature. However, you must be careful, as its hunger for other pets is as great as a Chafer''s perversion during a full moon.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7520,'en','A retired toy soldier, this metal creature suddenly came to life one day. It will follow you everywhere you go, risking its life to save yours. All you have to do in return is feed the little guy. This doesn''t mean he''ll fight your fights for you, though... he''ll never replace those naive Astrubian adventurers!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000016,'en','A retired toy soldier, this metal creature suddenly came to life one day. It will follow you everywhere you go, risking its life to save yours. All you have to do in return is feed the little guy. This doesn''t mean he''ll fight your fights for you, though... he''ll never replace those naive Astrubian adventurers!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000017,'en','A retired toy soldier, this metal creature suddenly came to life one day. It will follow you everywhere you go, risking its life to save yours. All you have to do in return is feed the little guy. This doesn''t mean he''ll fight your fights for you, though... he''ll never replace those naive Astrubian adventurers!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000018,'en','A retired toy soldier, this metal creature suddenly came to life one day. It will follow you everywhere you go, risking its life to save yours. All you have to do in return is feed the little guy. This doesn''t mean he''ll fight your fights for you, though... he''ll never replace those naive Astrubian adventurers!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000019,'en','A retired toy soldier, this metal creature suddenly came to life one day. It will follow you everywhere you go, risking its life to save yours. All you have to do in return is feed the little guy. This doesn''t mean he''ll fight your fights for you, though... he''ll never replace those naive Astrubian adventurers!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000020,'en','A retired toy soldier, this metal creature suddenly came to life one day. It will follow you everywhere you go, risking its life to save yours. All you have to do in return is feed the little guy. This doesn''t mean he''ll fight your fights for you, though... he''ll never replace those naive Astrubian adventurers!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7522,'en','Tamed and cleaned, this baby Minimino can be fed and petted without the loss of fingers, hands or elbow bones. You should remain careful though, as sometimes nature can reclaim control of its tamed manners. There is nothing worse than a Minimino being itself. To be safe, feed it only very rarely and beat it regularly with... well anything hard. Just treat him like you would your own child and everything might be fine.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7523,'en','No tomcat can resist this lovely ginger creature... not even the most happily married of them!
(THIS LEGENDARY PET DOES NOT NEED TO EAT).');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7524,'en','This surprising creature is the result of crossbreeding between a White Bow Meow and a Black Bow Meow. It only eats fish.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7552,'en','Sometimes, when true love joins a warrior and a Dragoturkey, weird things can happen. This cape proves it since there are Dragoturkey wings sewn on it. The Dragoturkey sacrificed itself for the making of this cape offered to the famous minstrel Pol Akartney on their wedding day. Apparently Jon Lemon even wrote a song about it.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7553,'en','If you ever dreamt of looking like a turkey, this is your chance! However, if you want to remain healthy, we advise you not to wear this hat on the streets of Amakna during the Christmas season.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7554,'en','Your friends are definitely going to be jealous. Those boots will take you all the way to the ambassador''s party for one of those wonderful little golden chocolates.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7555,'en','Gobble, gobble.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7559,'en','Legend has it that the very first owner of this belt used to spin round and round every time he put it on.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7581,'en','This bag looks just like a magic pineapple... maybe it''s a magic pineapple that turned into a bag for some reason. It has happened before. Unlike the Cawwot bag, the pineapple bag has not been hollowed out, so you can''t put anything in it. And it''s very heavy. Contrary to ''popular belief'', this bag is not part of the famous Pineapple set. Yes, I lied to you once again. Hahaha. I love this job.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7650,'en','This hammer opens up a whole new world of DIY to the family-oriented warrior.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7680,'en','This headgear is nothing but a piece of Ougaa''s head. Ougaa was a great divinity venerated by the Porcos. Padded with fabric, feathers and wool, anyone can wear this headgear, provided that they can stand the smell and the weight of it.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7702,'en','This Bow Wow is in a class of its own. The result of generations of breeding, it''s a noble-blooded hunting hound. Its extraordinary nose and perky yelping will help you flush out the biggest game in the forest... It will equally help the biggest game flush you out of the forest... Use with care.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7703,'en','This dark bird is especially renowned for its love of cemeteries and white-skinned adventurers. It loves to break the bones it finds in graves with its huge beak.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000004,'en','This dark bird is especially renowned for its love of cemeteries and white-skinned adventurers. It loves to break the bones it finds in graves with its huge beak.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7704,'en','This squirrel is a real acorn twister. It''ll tickle your monkey nuts one minute and break ''em the next. The crazy thing only eats seed.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7705,'en','This magnificent creature is somehow related to the famous Lenalds from Wabbit Island. More reckless and a lot more unruly, it will help you in combat but will prove incredibly deceitful if you don''t treat it well. This creature only eats meat.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7706,'en','Bilby, short for Bilbiblabaloo, is a little jelly in search of big adventures. Particularly attached to Vald, it has remarkable powers for its size due to its strict diet of flowers.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7707,'en','This wild little piggy has an immeasurably large snout, adapted to sniffing out acorns. It seemed to find you quite easily. This devourer of souls feeds off the remains of Lousy Pigs, piglets and boars.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7708,'en','This little Piwin is not like the others, one look at its colour and that is clear. However, it seems to share the same inexplicable interest in pecking posteriors. Don''t be shocked when I tell you that some people actually enjoy being aggressed by the little creatures. This pet only eats seeds.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000007,'en','This little Piwin is not like the others, one look at its colour and that is clear. However, it seems to share the same inexplicable interest in pecking posteriors. Don''t be shocked when I tell you that some people actually enjoy being aggressed by the little creatures. This pet only eats seeds.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(7709,'en','This little Piwin is not like the others, one look at its colour and that is clear. However, it seems to share the same inexplicable interest in pecking posteriors. Don''t be shocked when I tell you that some people actually enjoy being aggressed by the little creatures. This pet only eats seeds.');
