INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10948,'en','This shield shows all other adventurers that you were a pioneer in establishing your profession.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10949,'en','This shield shows all other adventurers that you were a pioneer in establishing your profession.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10950,'en','This shield shows all other adventurers that you were a pioneer in establishing your profession.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10951,'en','This shield shows all other adventurers that you were a pioneer in establishing your profession.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10952,'en','This shield shows all other adventurers that you were a pioneer in establishing your profession.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10953,'en','This shield shows all other adventurers that you were a pioneer in establishing your profession.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10954,'en','This shield shows all other adventurers that you were a pioneer in establishing your profession.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10955,'en','There''s nothing unusual about a bird being ringed!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10956,'en','Like the rest of the Black Crow set, this pair of boots has been passed down, foot to foot, through the generations. That explains the strong smell of Clakoss...');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10957,'en','Some thread, a needle, a few feathers taken from the remains of decaying Crows, and voilà! You''re in possession of the most chic of cloaks!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10958,'en','You can''t hide, you''ve been unmasked! So, the Black Crow is you after all! You would have gotten away with it too, if it weren''t for those meddling kids!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10959,'en','It might have taken you a while, but here it is, in your hands at last: the Black Crow''s Lance!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10962,'en','There''s nothing better than this staff for unblocking drains, or the nostrils of your fallen opponents. This weapon is still imbued with Plunder''s magic. You may be able to successfully embody him if you equip it.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10963,'en','The sole of these boots is spongy, so can absorb sewage sludge and release it again at every step, allowing you to retrace your steps easily.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10964,'en','Plunder hung his booty from this belt. You can make out a small valve on the inside. This valve allows the belt to be inflated, transforming it into a buoy. An essential item when venturing into the sewers.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10965,'en','This amulet was specially designed not to get stuck in Plunder''s neck hairs, so you can wear it without fear under your armpit or even keep it in your hand.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10971,'en','With this bag slung at a jaunty angle over your shoulder, you''ll be able to muck about while still keeping that charming smile on your face, you cheeky little monkey!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10975,'en','It might smell of stale Champmane but there''s nothing stale about this sword''s blade. This weapon is still imbued with Phong Huss''s magic. You may be able to successfully embody him if you equip it.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10976,'en','Fungi generally have collars, but Phong Huss preferred rings, possibly so that he could boast about having fingers.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10977,'en','Phong Huss wore this belt somewhat sloppily. He tried to wear it as a shoulder strap so he could sheath his sword in it. The belt pinched his nipples on multiple occasions, but other than that, was of no use whatsoever.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10978,'en','The feet of fungi are rarely very clean - they are often covered with mycelium. Phong Huss''s feet were no exception to this rule and he took care to hide them with his boots. They don''t smell particularly good, but they are well suited for growing mushrooms. Which of your stomach or your nose will win?');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10979,'en','Ektope took great pleasure in dragging this weapon behind him. He was well-known for being as lazy as a Gobball, but he mainly wanted to warn his opponents of his sensational arrival. This weapon is still imbued with Ektope''s magic. You may be able to successfully embody him if you equip it.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10980,'en','This ghost''s amulet must be extremely powerful, if one believes the legends about ghosts, that is.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10981,'en','It''s a well-known fact that real ghosts don''t have fingers. So how does that explain this ring?');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10982,'en','A drunken Captain Kradoc once stumbled into Ektope leaving a party at the Ripate Inn. "Ectoplasm on skates!" he ejaculated. Poor Captain Kradoc, the alcohol was playing tricks on him, Ektope has never had wheels.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10985,'en','This Bow Meow has known the winter of the far north, even if it has never actually seen the far north. Nobody knows how it arrived in Amakna, although the elders claim that it was imported from the island of Frigost to counter the ever-expanding Wabbit population. As such, this soul devourer will only eat Wabbits.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000065,'en','This Bow Meow has known the winter of the far north, even if it has never actually seen the far north. Nobody knows how it arrived in Amakna, although the elders claim that it was imported from the island of Frigost to counter the ever-expanding Wabbit population. As such, this soul devourer will only eat Wabbits.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10987,'en','This belt cools the hips, organs and ardour of all those who dare to wear it. To be given to your most stubborn suitors.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10988,'en','This hat is ideal for keeping your head cool and your ideas fresh. That said, if you don''t want to look like an ugly ice cube, you''ll have to find something else.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10989,'en','Jon Lemon wore a similar cape during his famous concert in Brouce Boulgoure''s Clearing. Those who weren''t deafened still remember the concert''s climax, when he stopped singing after becoming trapped in the ice because of his own cape.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10990,'en','Heavy and stiff, these boots don''t look particularly special, but their icy sole will have you ice-skating without the need for ice. Of course, you''ll need to find a surface covered with ice-skate blades, but in these crazy times, that shouldn''t be too difficult.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(11011,'en','Crazier than a regular Minifoux but much less ginger, this pet can swim underwater without needing to plug its nose.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000014,'en','Crazier than a regular Minifoux but much less ginger, this pet can swim underwater without needing to plug its nose.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(11049,'en','Grillian was a great magician. Having forgotten how to make Vanishing Powder, he successfully reinvented it. He never did find the missing half of his assistant, though.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(11050,'en','This cape is supposed to protect your posterior from the bites of carnivorous plants.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(11051,'en','Grillian wore this amulet around his neck when... When... What does it matter? He died and now this amulet is yours.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(11052,'en','Grillian the magician traded a magic ring for this pair of boots. It seems he lost out on the deal as they aren''t even padded.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(11055,'en','Gadjet was one of the most creative handymen in the World of 12. Unfortunately he was also one of the most absent-minded. They say he mixed up his anvil and the head of his wife more than once and she did not complain.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(11056,'en','Gadjet made this cape hoping it might enable him to fly and thus more easily escape the punishment administered daily by his wife.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(11057,'en','By wearing this belt upside down and pressing on it hard enough, you may be able to activate the integrated retromagic module. It has never worked, but you can activate it anyway. You can then sell it to someone as naive as you.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(11058,'en','Worn by several generations of handymen, this ring will protect you from striking your knuckle with your hammer. Unfortunately, it is never sold in packs of five.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(11465,'en','A lover of Goblimps'' warped sense of humor, Komet was charmed by your own, and decided to leave the snowy forests of Kwismas Island so he could accompany you on many a rousing adventure. What''s his secret to making his magnificent antlers grow back so quickly after shedding? "Wood" you believe it''s eating... wood! The harder on the teeth, the bigger the antlers!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(10000048,'en','A lover of Goblimps'' warped sense of humor, Komet was charmed by your own, and decided to leave the snowy forests of Kwismas Island so he could accompany you on many a rousing adventure. What''s his secret to making his magnificent antlers grow back so quickly after shedding? "Wood" you believe it''s eating... wood! The harder on the teeth, the bigger the antlers!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(11471,'en','This cloak is very special indeed, as it allows its wearer to display anything at all on his or her back. Most dumb adventurers just use it to show off hunting trophies and count how many people are taking an interest in them, but a few canny wearers have managed to generate a real following with their original ideas.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(11472,'en','When wearing this shield, you will be visible from afar. This allows anyone to keep tabs on your exhilarating adventures and know where you are at all times, including any stops you make at Astrub Inn.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(11473,'en','This thing can talk... And talk... And talk... And talk! It picks up phrases it likes and repeats them to Witter Beanies in the area. At first, these hats were quite a good alternative to carrier pigeons, until they became so commonly used that the same messages started going round and round in circles, resulting in a permanent hubbub. These days they''re also used for a parlour game called Rage K-Witter in which each participant dons a Witter Beanie and the one who can stand the noise the longest is pronounced the winner.');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(11476,'en','This familiar-looking headgear was enchanted by Hel Munster himself after a famous Astrubian fashion designer wouldn''t stop asking him. He wanted to offer a collection that adjusted to the colours of the person wearing it. Despite its being discoloured by a top-secret process, you can still recognise the unmistakable smell of Boowolf slobber emanating from it... Yuck!');
INSERT INTO "item_descriptions" VALUES(11477,'en','This familiar-looking headgear was enchanted by Hel Munster himself after a famous Astrubian fashion designer wouldn''t stop asking him. He wanted to offer a collection that adjusted to the colours of the person wearing it. Despite its being discoloured by a top-secret process, you can still recognise the unmistakable smell of Boowolf slobber emanating from it... Yuck!');
